//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MummyTKT's Bias Pointer v11 — live alerts + on-chart labels (2026-10-27)
//
// The logic proven in the backtest edition is now the live logic. Every bias
// alert also puts an "H4 aligned - Alert" label on that H4 candle (each display
// item can be switched off under "Chart labels"), filtered like Alert Filters:
//   Origin (BUY / SELL CONFIRMED)   External on, Internal off
//   H4 back in line                 External on, Internal off
//   H4 breakout in line, Breaker Origin / retest, OC reaction, Engulfing (wick)
// Continuations follow the setup's latest H4 confirmation (External / Internal).
//
// Since v7:
//   • Daily V-shapes (A-shapes for sells) formed after the Daily breakout,
//     beyond the Daily Breaker, are reaction levels while the direction holds
//     (they die on a Daily close through them, like every Daily level).
//   • A fresh Daily reaction followed by an H4 breakout alerts EVERY time,
//     also while H4 is still aligned after the Origin:
//     "Daily reaction + H4 breakout". Each fresh reaction after a confirmation
//     starts its own External / Internal check.
//   • A new Daily breakout in the SAME direction doesn't reset H4: in-line
//     breakouts and H4 reactions keep firing. A reaction at the new breakout's
//     Daily levels + an H4 breakout then becomes what H4 rides on. Only a Daily
//     breakout the other way resets H4.
//
// Since v8 (FVGs):
//   • Daily FVGs are reaction levels: inside the range that was just broken
//     ("inside_fvg") and reaching beyond the Daily Breaker ("post_breakout_fvg").
//     A gap is an FVG once its third Daily candle closes without reaching the
//     first (the middle one can be the breakout candle). An H4 wick entering the
//     gap is a reaction; only a Daily CLOSE through the gap kills it. While price
//     reacts inside it, each Daily candle that dips below the previous Daily low
//     (above the high for sells) restarts the External check from when that
//     candle entered the gap. Other Daily levels keep the first-touch rule.
//   • H4 FVG after an H4 breakout in line (Origin, Daily reaction + H4 breakout,
//     back in line, in line): the NEXT H4 candle is checked once; if it completes
//     an FVG one alert is sent: cont_type "h4_fvg" ("<PAIR> / H4 FVG candle
//     after breakout has formed", no buy / sell).
//
// v11 rule (2026-10-27): a used level is used. Only the first touch of a level
//   counts: a Daily level (Breaker, OC, V/A-shape, FVG) that has given its H4
//   confirmation never starts another reaction; the H4 Breaker and H4 OCs are
//   used by their first touch (alert only if that touch is a rejection). The
//   one exception: while price reacts inside a Daily FVG, a deeper Daily candle
//   moves the External start to that candle (before the alert). A reaction that
//   fails (an H4 close back through the level) uses the level too. External =
//   the last H4 A (V for sells) formed BEFORE the candle that touched / entered
//   the level; an A / V completed by that candle or later is Internal.
//
// v11 display: confirmation alerts are small arrows; an engulfing is a box over its two
//   candles with a "D" / "H4" pointer, own colours, last N of each (Daily on D and
//   lower, H4 on 4H and lower: the same boxes as on 4H); the H4 FVG is a dot with
//   its own table row, so nothing replaces the latest confirmation arrow; alerts are small arrows / dots on the triggering candle (hover for the
//   details); the alert text and the status sit in an info table at the side
//   ("Alert marks on the chart" = Full labels brings the old labels back).
//
// v11 (2026-10-27): Daily engulfing in the current Daily direction alerts
//   (cont_type "d_engulfing", eng_wick like the H4 engulfing; any time a Daily
//   direction is set). A notification only: "<PAIR> / Daily engulfing candle
//   has formed", no buy / sell. The Weekly follows every Daily rule (used
//   levels too). Settings are grouped under numbered, titled sections.
//
// v12 (2026-10-27): OC formed notifications (no buy / sell). Daily: at the Daily
//   close, the last two Daily candles both in the current Daily direction
//   (cont_type "d_oc_formed", level = the first one's close). H4: after the
//   Origin while H4 is in line, the last two H4 candles both in the Daily
//   direction (cont_type "h4_oc_formed"). On the chart an "✕" marks the newest
//   of each (Daily on D and lower, H4 on 4H); not in the info table.
//
// v12 option (2026-10-28) "H4 OC only after a retest that held": after each H4
//   breakout in line (Origin, Daily reaction + H4 breakout, back in line, in line)
//   the H4 OC rejection and H4 OC formed only start counting after an H4 candle has
//   touched the H4 Breaker, or an H4 V-shape (A-shape for sells) of the breakout
//   leg below it (above it for sells), and closed back beyond it. Each new H4
//   breakout in line starts over. The alerts carry "after_retest"; each person
//   picks it in Alert Filters, the chart setting only picks the chart marks.
//
// v10 display: each H4 breakout after a Daily reaction says on its chart label
//   whether an H4 candle swept an H4 swing low (high, sells) during the break
//   ("Sweep check on H4 breakout labels"; display only, no alert), and every
//   H4 sweep is marked like LuxAlgo ("Show every H4 sweep").
//
// Since v10: the Weekly follows the Daily rules one level up (first Daily touch
//   decides External / Internal, Weekly V/A after the breakout, Weekly FVGs with
//   every Daily FVG rule, the breakout Week's close counts as moving away, a
//   Weekly-confirmed Daily breakout uses up the Weekly reaction). The Weekly
//   still never fires an alert; it labels the Daily setup.
//
// Since v9 (which Daily FVG counts):
//   • A bullish FVG only reacts when price DIPS INTO it from above (a bearish one
//     from below). Once price has traded past its far edge it can't start a new
//     reaction; a reaction already running there lives until a Daily close.
//   • While reacting at an FVG, price entering a DEEPER FVG moves the reaction
//     there, with that FVG's own External level.
//   • Each FVG keeps its own External level (from the candle that first entered
//     it, moved by each deeper Daily candle while it is the reaction); a return
//     to it uses that level, not the H4 A/V formed at the return.
//   • An H4 breakout from an FVG uses up the FVGs above it (below, for sells)
//     that price went through, and the FVG itself.
//
// The label sits on the candle that CLOSED to confirm: entry = next candle's open.
// Daily data is read from completed candles only, so history doesn't repaint.
// The "Internal H4 breakouts" switch also decides whether Internal confirmations
// are SENT: off (default) = only External breakouts confirm a reaction.
//
//
// Apply to a 4H chart for each instrument.
// Create ONE alert per instrument: condition = "Any alert() function call"
//                                   webhook  = https://forex-radar.fly.dev/api/tv-webhook
//
// Event types:
//   BREAKOUT         — Daily candle closed beyond the most recent external
//                      high/low (level_type "external")
//   RETEST           — H4 entered a reaction source zone
//   RETEST_CANCELLED — H4 moved away from zone without H4 confirmation
//   CONFIRMED        — H4 closed beyond an H4 A/V level during a daily retest (Origin)
//   INVALIDATED      — no longer sent: a break the other way is a new BREAKOUT
//   H4_CONTINUATION  — H4 continuation event after Origin has fired
//                      cont_type: breakout_cont | daily_react | inline_break | breaker_origin | breaker_cont | oc_cont | engulfing | h4_fvg | d_engulfing | d_oc_formed | h4_oc_formed
//   PRICE_UPDATE     — Current H4 close price, powers dashboard price-level alerts
//
// v5 change: added PRICE_UPDATE event — fires at every realtime H4 close.
// 2026-10-16: every completed post-breakout daily OC is watched (not just the
//             latest) until an opposing breakout; a daily-zone reaction stays
//             valid on later candles — any later H4 close beyond the H4 A/V
//             confirms it — and only fails on an H4 close back through the zone.
//            Backend uses it to check subscriber price-level alerts.
// 2026-10-16 (b): daily candles read with lookahead_on (history no longer a day
//             late after a paste); pip sizes match the server's table; every
//             webhook carries "timeframe"; PRICE_UPDATE carries a chart snapshot
//             (stage + all levels); "moved away first" can't be inherited from
//             the previous breakout; External/Internal is judged against the
//             CURRENT reaction's start (also after a failed reaction restarts).
// 2026-10-18: daily bias comes from market structure — external, internal and
//             inner internal highs/lows (wick levels, body-close breaks, no
//             tolerance). The most recent break on any layer is the breakout;
//             its level is the breaker and the rest of that range is the
//             inside-range zone. D.A/D.V are wick levels and only the one in line
//             with the bias is shown (D.V for buys, D.A for sells).
// 2026-10-19: retest and H4-aligned chart markers removed. Layers replaced by
//             ONE most-recent external high/low: structures form inside the
//             current range at any depth (same rules) and only the newest pair
//             is drawn; its latest break is the daily breakout.
//             H4 Breaker / H4 OC continuations only count a candle that OPENS on
//             the bias side of the level (a climb through it from below — or a
//             drop through it from above for sells — is not a rejection).
//             Reactions must touch the level exactly (no ±tolerance on the
//             touch). H4 is out of line on a close beyond the LATEST H4 V (buy)
//             / A (sell); that drops every H4 OC until H4 breaks back in line,
//             and an H4 OC closed through against the bias is dropped.
//             Inside-range reactions must come from a Daily V-shape (A-shape for
//             sells) or Daily OC level inside the broken range: exact touch, hold;
//             the reaction fails on a close through that level.
//             H4 out of line → H4 only realigns after a FRESH daily reaction
//             (same three zones), then an H4 break; the alert names that level.
//             External/Internal is judged from the first reaction at the daily
//             level that confirms (a failed reaction restarting there keeps it).
//             H4 OCs: every OC of the latest H4 breakout leg (and after it) is
//             watched; each alerts once on a rejection then is removed; checked
//             before a new candle can form the next OC; all dropped when H4
//             breaks the other way or on a new daily breakout.
//             Daily levels (structure, D.A/D.V, inside-range V/A) come from
//             candle BODIES by default; setting "Daily levels from" = Wick
//             restores the wick levels.
//             Daily reaction levels (V/A-shapes, Daily OCs, post-breakout OCs)
//             die once a Daily candle closes through them; dead levels never
//             count as a reaction again.
//             While H4 is in line, every new H4 close beyond the latest H4 A
//             (buy) / V (sell) alerts ("H4 breakout in line with the Daily"); its
//             level becomes the H4 Breaker and its leg's OCs are kept.
//             Webhooks carry the exchange (syminfo.prefix); on Deriv synthetic
//             indices and crypto one pip is 0.002% of price (5-pip allowance = 0.01%).
//             PRICE_UPDATE carries the closed H4 candle and the last Daily candle;
//             each new alert first sends 40 Daily then 40 H4 candles (HISTORY)
//             for the server's chart pictures.
//             Weekly storyline: Weekly External breakout → Weekly reaction (on
//             Daily candles) → Daily breakout in the Weekly direction is
//             Weekly-confirmed (Internal / External); bias alerts carry wk_* fields.
//             H4 engulfing (body covers the previous opposite body; eng_wick when it
//             also closes beyond that candle's wick) after the
//             Origin, in line, in the Daily direction: cont_type "engulfing".
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

indicator("Backtest", overlay=true, max_bars_back=2000, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500)

// ── Settings, in titled sections (the group titles are the headers in TradingView) ─
const string G_SETUP = "1 · Setup and connection"
const string G_ALERT = "2 · Alerts and chart labels (same switches as Alert Filters)"
const string G_ENG   = "3 · Engulfing and OC formed (H4 and Daily)"
const string G_DLVL  = "4 · Daily levels and FVGs"
const string GS1     = "5 · Daily External high / low"
const string G_WK    = "6 · Weekly"
const string G_SW    = "7 · H4 liquidity sweeps (display only)"
const string G_BT    = "8 · Backtest: start date, label style, count table"
const string G_LBL   = "9 · Right-edge level labels and lines"
const string GLC     = "10 · Label colours (use the opacity slider to fade them)"

// 1 · Setup and connection
string wh_secret       = input.string("", "Webhook Secret", group=G_SETUP,
     tooltip="Paste your TV_WEBHOOK_SECRET value here")
int    tol_pips        = input.int(5, "Tolerance Pips", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_SETUP,
     tooltip="Half-width of the reaction zone band in pips")

// 2 · Alerts and chart labels
bool   bt_show     = input.bool(true,  "Show alert labels on the chart", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_ext      = input.bool(true,  "External H4 breakouts", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_int      = input.bool(false, "Internal H4 breakouts", group=G_ALERT,
     tooltip="Off: only an External H4 breakout confirms a Daily reaction, and only those are sent. On: Internal ones are sent too.")
bool   bt_origin   = input.bool(true,  "Origin — BUY / SELL CONFIRMED", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_react    = input.bool(true,  "Daily reaction + H4 breakout (after the Origin)", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_realign  = input.bool(true,  "H4 back in line", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_inline   = input.bool(true,  "H4 breakout in line", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_breaker  = input.bool(true,  "H4 Breaker (first touch)", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_oc       = input.bool(true,  "H4 OC reaction", group=G_ALERT)
bool   bt_oc_rt    = input.bool(false, "H4 OC only after a retest that held", group=G_ALERT,
     tooltip="On: after each H4 breakout in line, H4 OC rejections and H4 OC formed wait until an H4 candle has touched the H4 Breaker, or an H4 V-shape (A-shape for sells) of the breakout leg, and closed back beyond it. From then on every one shows, until the next H4 breakout in line, which waits for its own retest. Off = every H4 OC rejection / OC formed, as before. Chart only; Alert Filters has the same switch for your alerts.")
bool   bt_h4fvg    = input.bool(true,  "H4 FVG after an H4 breakout", group=G_ALERT,
     tooltip="After an Origin, Daily reaction + H4 breakout, H4 back in line or H4 breakout in line: if the NEXT H4 candle completes an FVG (buys: its low stays above the high of the candle before the breakout), one alert. Checked once per breakout.")

// 3 · Engulfing
bool   bt_engulf   = input.bool(true,  "H4 engulfing", group=G_ENG, inline="h4e")
string bt_eng_mode = input.string("Wick", "covers", options=["Wick", "Body only", "Both"], group=G_ENG, inline="h4e",
     tooltip="After the Origin, while H4 is in line: an H4 candle covering the previous opposite candle, in the Daily direction. Wick: it also closes beyond that candle's wick. The alert is always sent; each person picks Wick / Body / Both in Alert Filters. This only picks the chart labels.")
bool   bt_dengulf  = input.bool(true,  "Daily engulfing", group=G_ENG, inline="d1e")
string bt_deng_mode = input.string("Wick", "covers", options=["Wick", "Body only", "Both"], group=G_ENG, inline="d1e",
     tooltip="A Daily candle covering the previous opposite Daily candle, in the current Daily direction (buys: the previous Daily candle is bearish; this one opens at or below its close and closes above its open; Wick = also above its high). The alert is always sent; each person picks Wick / Body / Both in Alert Filters. This only picks the chart labels.")

color  bt_engh_col = input.color(color.new(#4FC3F7, 0), "H4 engulfing box", group=G_ENG, inline="ebh")
int    eng_n_h     = input.int(1, "keep the last", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_ENG, inline="ebh",
     tooltip="H4 engulfings are boxed on the 4H chart and every lower timeframe (1H, 15m, ...), with an 'H4' pointer under the box. Below 4H the same boxes as on the 4H chart are shown (the alerted ones: after the Origin, H4 in line). The box marks the covered candle (the bearish one in a bullish engulfing): Wick = its wick, for engulfings that close beyond that wick; Body only = from its body to its last point in the move (buys: body top down to its low; sells: body bottom up to its high), for every engulfing (one that covers the wick covers the body too); Both = every engulfing, the Wick box when the wick was covered, else the Body box. Keep the last = how many of the most recent stay on the chart.")
color  bt_engd_col = input.color(color.new(#FFD54F, 0), "Daily engulfing box", group=G_ENG, inline="ebd")
int    eng_n_d     = input.int(1, "keep the last", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_ENG, inline="ebd",
     tooltip="Daily engulfings are boxed on the Daily chart and every lower timeframe (4H, 1H, ...), with a 'D' pointer under the box. The 'covers' choice decides the box, as for H4. Keep the last = how many of the most recent stay on the chart.")
bool   bt_docf     = input.bool(true, "Daily OC formed ✕", group=G_ENG, inline="ocf")
bool   bt_hocf     = input.bool(true, "H4 OC formed ✕", group=G_ENG, inline="ocf",
     tooltip="An ✕ on the newest OC formed (two candles in a row in the Daily direction; level = where the first one closed). Daily: any time a Daily direction is set, on the Daily chart and lower. H4: after the Origin while H4 is in line, on the 4H chart. Only the most recent of each is shown. The notification is always sent; each person switches it on or off in Alert Filters. Not in the info table.")
color  bt_ocf_col  = input.color(color.new(#E040FB, 0), "OC formed ✕", group=G_ENG)

// 4 · Daily levels and FVGs
bool   d_body = input.string("Body", "Daily levels from", options = ["Body", "Wick"], group = G_DLVL,
     tooltip = "Body: Daily highs/lows, A-shapes and V-shapes use candle bodies, like H4. Wick: they use the wicks. A breakout is always a Daily close beyond the level. Each alert keeps the setting it was created with.") == "Body"
bool   bt_dfvg     = input.bool(true,  "Daily FVGs as reaction levels", group=G_DLVL,
     tooltip="Bullish Daily FVGs (bearish for sells) inside the range that was just broken, or formed after the breakout beyond the Daily Breaker. An H4 wick entering the gap is a reaction. Each Daily candle that dips below the previous Daily low inside it (above the high for sells) restarts the External check from when that candle entered the gap. A Daily close through the gap kills it. The gap only exists once its third candle has closed; the middle candle can be the Daily breakout candle.")
bool   bt_lvls     = input.bool(true,  "Show the Daily reaction levels being watched (4H)", group=G_DLVL,
     tooltip="Every Daily level the script would accept a reaction at right now. A level that is missing here can't trigger an alert.")
color  bt_lv_col   = input.color(color.new(color.aqua, 25), "Daily levels watched", group=G_DLVL, inline="dlc")
color  bt_fvg_col  = input.color(color.new(color.aqua, 85), "Daily FVGs watched", group=G_DLVL, inline="dlc")

// 5 · Daily External high / low
bool   show_ext = input.bool(true, "Show external high / low", group = GS1)
color  c_eh  = input.color(#E0E0E0, "External high", group = GS1, inline = "eh")
string s_eh  = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group = GS1, inline = "eh")
color  c_el  = input.color(#E0E0E0, "External low ", group = GS1, inline = "el")
string s_el  = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group = GS1, inline = "el")
int    w_ext = input.int(2, "Line width", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = GS1)
color  bt_ext_txt   = input.color(#E0E0E0, "External high / low text", group = GS1)

// 6 · Weekly
bool   bt_weekly   = input.bool(false, "Weekly (lines, labels, Weekly AGAINST marks)", group=G_WK,
     tooltip="Off: Daily + H4 only. The Weekly never changes which alerts fire; it only adds context.")
bool   w_body = input.string("Body", "Weekly levels from", options = ["Body", "Wick"], group = G_WK,
     tooltip = "Body: Weekly highs/lows, A-shapes and V-shapes use candle bodies. Wick: they use the wicks. Set separately from the Daily choice.") == "Body"
bool   show_wk_lbls     = input.bool(true, "Show Weekly labels (W.BK / W.A / W.V / W.OC)",
     tooltip="Right-edge labels for the Weekly Breaker, Weekly A/V-shape and post-breakout Weekly OC",
     group=G_WK)
bool   show_wk_ext      = input.bool(true, "Show Weekly External high / low lines", group=G_WK)
color  wk_col           = input.color(#FFB74D, "Weekly lines & labels color", group=G_WK)
string wk_style         = input.string("Dashed", "Weekly External line style", options=["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group=G_WK)
int    wk_width         = input.int(2, "Weekly External line width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=G_WK)
string wk_lbl_max_tf    = input.string("Daily", "Weekly labels & lines visible on",
     options=["Monthly", "Weekly", "Daily", "4H", "1H", "30m", "15m", "5m"],
     tooltip="Weekly level labels and lines appear on this timeframe and all lower timeframes.",
     group=G_WK)

// 7 · H4 liquidity sweeps
bool   bt_sweep    = input.bool(true, "Sweep check on H4 breakout labels", group=G_SW,
     tooltip="Display only. On each H4 breakout after a Daily reaction, the label says whether an H4 candle swept an H4 swing low (high, for sells) during that break: a wick beyond it with the close back. Swings and sweeps are found like LuxAlgo's Liquidity Sweeps (wicks only).")
int    sw_len      = input.int(5, "Sweep: swing length (candles each side)", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_SW)
color  sw_col      = input.color(color.new(#7048e8, 20), "Sweep line on breakout labels", group=G_SW)
bool   sw_all      = input.bool(true, "Show every H4 sweep (like LuxAlgo)", group=G_SW,
     tooltip="Display only. Marks every H4 sweep on the chart: a dotted line from the swing to the sweep candle and a zone over the wick that swept it. Off: only the breakout labels say whether a sweep came first.")
color  sw_bull_col = input.color(color.new(#089981, 70), "Bullish sweep zone", group=G_SW, inline="swz")
color  sw_bear_col = input.color(color.new(#F23645, 70), "Bearish sweep zone", group=G_SW, inline="swz")
bool   sw_ext      = input.bool(true, "Extend sweep zones", group=G_SW, inline="swe",
     tooltip="On: each zone stretches right until a candle closes through it (or the max bars). Off: the zone stays on the sweep candle.")
int    sw_maxb     = input.int(300, "max bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_SW, inline="swe")
string sw_lmode    = input.string("Swing to sweep", "Sweep lines (dotted)", options=["Swing to sweep", "Extend right", "Hide"], group=G_SW,
     tooltip="The dotted line from the swing high / low to the candle that swept it. Extend right: runs on to the right edge. Hide: zones only.")

// 8 · Backtest: start date, label style, count table
int    bt_from     = input.time(timestamp("2020-01-01T00:00:00"), "Backtest from", group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Labels and counts start at this date. Earlier candles still build the levels.")
bool   bt_latest   = input.bool(true,  "Keep only the latest alert label (clean chart)", group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Each new alert label deletes the previous one. The count table still counts every alert. Switch off to see the whole history.")
bool   bt_grey     = input.bool(true,  "Show alerts that are not counted (grey, with the reason)", group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Alerts before the start date, Internal ones while Internal is off, and types switched off above.")
bool   bt_table    = input.bool(true,  "Show count table", group=G_BT)
string bt_marks    = input.string("Circle + info table", "Alert marks on the chart", options=["Circle + info table", "Full labels"], group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Circle + info table: each alert is a small arrow or dot on the candle that triggered it (hover it for the details); the alert text and the status go in a table at the side, so the candles stay clear. Full labels: the old text labels on the chart.")
string bt_mark_shape = input.string("Small arrow", "Mark shape", options=["Small arrow", "Dot"], group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Small arrow: ▲ under a buy candle, ▼ over a sell candle. Dot: a small dot. Only on the candle that triggered the alert; hover it for the details.")
bool   bt_info_on  = input.bool(true, "Show info table (status + latest alert)", group=G_BT,
     tooltip="Off hides the table at the side of the chart. Alerts, marks and boxes are not affected.")
string bt_info_pos = input.string("Top right", "Info table position", options=["Top right", "Middle right", "Bottom right", "Top left", "Middle left", "Bottom left"], group=G_BT)
color  bt_buy_col  = input.color(#00C853, "Buy label", group=G_BT, inline="btc")
color  bt_sell_col = input.color(#FF1744, "Sell label", group=G_BT, inline="btc")
color  bt_txt_col  = input.color(color.white, "Label text", group=G_BT, inline="btc")
color  bt_grey_col = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 35), "Not-counted label", group=G_BT, inline="btg")
color  bt_h4fvg_col = input.color(color.new(#FF9800, 10), "H4 FVG label", group=G_BT, inline="btg")
color  bt_tbl_bg   = input.color(color.new(#0F1120, 10), "Table background", group=G_BT, inline="btt")
color  bt_tbl_txt  = input.color(color.white, "Table text", group=G_BT, inline="btt")
color  bt_state_txt = input.color(color.white, "Status label text", group=G_BT)

// 9 · Right-edge level labels and lines
bool   show_daily_lbls = input.bool(true,  "Show Daily labels (D.A / D.V / D.OC)",
     tooltip="Toggle right-edge labels for Daily A-shape, V-shape and OC levels",
     group=G_LBL)
bool   show_h4_lbls    = input.bool(true,  "Show H4 labels (H4.A / H4.V / H4.OC / H4.BK)",
     tooltip="Toggle right-edge labels for H4 formation and breaker levels",
     group=G_LBL)
bool   show_lvl_lines  = input.bool(false, "Show level lines (extend right)",
     tooltip="Draw a horizontal line from each level's origin extending to the right",
     group=G_LBL)
color  daily_line_col  = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 20), "Daily line color",
     tooltip="Color for D.A / D.V / D.OC lines",
     group=G_LBL)
color  h4_line_col     = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 40), "H4 line color",
     tooltip="Color for H4.A / H4.V / H4.OC / H4.BK lines",
     group=G_LBL)
string daily_lbl_max_tf = input.string("Daily", "Daily labels & lines visible on",
     options=["Monthly", "Weekly", "Daily", "4H", "1H", "30m", "15m", "5m"],
     tooltip="Daily level labels and lines appear on this timeframe and all lower timeframes. E.g. choose Weekly to also see them on the weekly chart.",
     group=G_LBL)
string h4_lbl_max_tf    = input.string("4H",    "H4 labels & lines visible on",
     options=["Monthly", "Weekly", "Daily", "4H", "1H", "30m", "15m", "5m"],
     tooltip="H4 level labels and lines appear on this timeframe and all lower timeframes. E.g. choose Daily to also see them on the daily chart.",
     group=G_LBL)

// 10 · Label colours
color  bull_lbl_col     = input.color(color.new(color.green, 60), "Bullish state label color",
     tooltip="Background color of the state label when direction is bullish (BREAKOUT / awaiting retest)",
     group=GLC)
color  bear_lbl_col     = input.color(color.new(color.red,   60), "Bearish state label color",
     tooltip="Background color of the state label when direction is bearish (BREAKOUT / awaiting retest)",
     group=GLC)
color  retest_lbl_col   = input.color(color.orange, "State label: Retest", group = GLC)
color  conf_lbl_col     = input.color(color.teal,   "State label: Confirmed · H4 aligned", group = GLC)
color  realign_lbl_col  = input.color(color.blue,   "State label: OUT OF LINE (H4 against daily)", group = GLC)
color  idle_lbl_col     = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 20), "State label: no breakout", group = GLC)
color  da_lbl_col       = input.color(color.new(color.red,    55), "D.A", group = GLC, inline = "dl")
color  dv_lbl_col       = input.color(color.new(color.lime,   45), "D.V", group = GLC, inline = "dl")
color  doc_lbl_col      = input.color(color.new(color.purple, 45), "D.OC", group = GLC, inline = "dl")
color  h4a_lbl_col      = input.color(color.new(color.red,    72), "H4.A", group = GLC, inline = "hl")
color  h4v_lbl_col      = input.color(color.new(color.lime,   65), "H4.V", group = GLC, inline = "hl")
color  h4bk_lbl_col     = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 25), "H4.BK", group = GLC, inline = "hl")
color  h4oc_lbl_col     = input.color(color.new(color.teal,   45), "H4.OC", group = GLC, inline = "hl")

// counts: 0 Origin, 1 Back in line, 2 In line, 3 Breaker Origin, 4 Breaker retest, 5 OC, 6 Engulfing,
//         7 Daily reaction + H4 breakout, 8 Buys, 9 Sells, 10 H4 FVG after breakout, 11 Daily engulfing
var bt_cnt  = array.new_int(12, 0)
var int bt_t0 = time
// External / Internal of the setup's latest H4 confirmation (Origin, Daily reaction
// + H4 breakout, or back in line); continuations follow it, like the server
var bt_scls = array.from("")
var bt_last = array.new<label>(2, na)   // the alert labels on the chart: 0 = confirmations, 1 = H4 FVG
// "H4 OC only after a retest that held": every H4 V / A formed (level, bar), the
// levels of the latest H4 breakout in line that count as its retest (the Breaker
// + the leg's V / A beyond it), and whether one was retested and held
var vh_lv = array.new<float>()
var vh_b  = array.new<int>()
var ah_lv = array.new<float>()
var ah_b  = array.new<int>()
var rt_lvls = array.new<float>()
var rt_held = array.from(false)
// The newest OC formed marks (✕): Daily, H4
var label ocf_d = na
var label ocf_h = na
// Engulfing boxes and pointers on the chart, oldest first (Daily / H4)
var eng_bd = array.new<box>()
var eng_ld = array.new<label>()
var eng_bh = array.new<box>()
var eng_lh = array.new<label>()
// The latest H4 engulfing boxed on the 4H chart: count, first candle's time, box, words
var int    e4_n    = 0
var int    e4_t1   = na
var float  e4_top  = na
var float  e4_bot  = na
var string e4_tip  = ""
// External / Internal of the setup's latest H4 confirmation, kept apart from the
// label code (bt_scls) so request.security can read e4_* (no drawings allowed there)
var string e4_cls  = ""
// Info table: the latest alert's text and when it fired (circle mode keeps the candles clear)
var bt_info = array.from("", "", "", "")   // text, time: confirmations (0, 1), H4 FVG (2, 3)
// The External H4 level of the current Daily reaction: the latest H4 A (buys) /
// V (sells) when the reaction started, i.e. formed BEFORE it
var float bt_ext_a = na
var float bt_ext_v = na
var bt_seen = array.new<float>()   // Daily levels already touched since they formed
// H4 liquidity sweeps (display only): live swing lows / highs and the sweeps seen
var array<float> sw_pl_p = array.new<float>()   // swing lows not yet closed through
var array<int>   sw_pl_b = array.new<int>()
var array<float> sw_ph_p = array.new<float>()   // swing highs not yet closed through
var array<int>   sw_ph_b = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   swb_bar = array.new<int>()     // bullish sweeps (wick below a swing low, close back above)
var array<float> swb_lvl = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   swb_piv = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   sws_bar = array.new<int>()     // bearish sweeps (wick above a swing high, close back below)
var array<float> sws_lvl = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   sws_piv = array.new<int>()
var array<line>  sw_lines = array.new<line>()
var array<line>  sw_all_l = array.new<line>()    // every sweep ("Show every H4 sweep")
var array<box>   sw_all_b = array.new<box>()
var array<bool>  sw_all_d = array.new<bool>()    // zone direction: true = bullish sweep
var array<bool>  sw_all_x = array.new<bool>()    // zone closed through (stops extending)
var string bt_swtxt = ""                         // sweep line for the breakout label being drawn
var BT_NAMES = array.from("Origin", "Back in line", "H4 breakout in line", "Breaker Origin", "Breaker retest", "OC reaction", "Engulfing", "Daily reaction + H4 breakout", "Buys", "Sells", "H4 FVG after breakout", "Daily engulfing")

f_style(string st) =>
    st == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : st == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

// ── Timeframe visibility helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────
f_tf_str(opt) =>
    switch opt
        "Monthly" => "M"
        "Weekly"  => "W"
        "Daily"   => "D"
        "4H"      => "240"
        "1H"      => "60"
        "30m"     => "30"
        "15m"     => "15"
        =>           "5"

bool show_daily_on_tf = timeframe.in_seconds() <= timeframe.in_seconds(f_tf_str(daily_lbl_max_tf))
bool show_h4_on_tf    = timeframe.in_seconds() <= timeframe.in_seconds(f_tf_str(h4_lbl_max_tf))
bool show_wk_on_tf    = timeframe.in_seconds() <= timeframe.in_seconds(f_tf_str(wk_lbl_max_tf))

// Pip size per market — must match pip_size_for() in config.py on the server.
// mintick × 10 is only right for forex; indices/crypto/oil use the server's table.
f_pip(string t) =>
    switch t
        "XAUUSD"  => 0.10
        "XAGUSD"  => 0.01
        "BTCUSD"  => 10.0
        "ETHUSD"  => 1.0
        "SOLUSD"  => 0.05
        "BNBUSD"  => 0.10
        "XRPUSD"  => 0.0002
        "ADAUSD"  => 0.00005
        "DOGEUSD" => 0.00002
        "LTCUSD"  => 0.02
        "WTIUSD"  => 0.05
        "US30"    => 10.0
        "NAS100"  => 5.0
        "SPX500"  => 2.0
        "UK100"   => 3.0
        "GER40"   => 5.0
        "JPN225"  => 10.0
        => str.endswith(t, "JPY") ? 0.01 : 0.0001

// Deriv synthetic indices have no pips: one "pip" is 0.002% of price, so the
// default 5-pip allowance is 0.01% of price.
bool  is_deriv = syminfo.prefix == "DERIV"
// Crypto too (any exchange: BTCUSDT on Binance never matched the table above)
bool  rel_pip  = is_deriv or syminfo.type == "crypto"
float pip = rel_pip ? close * 0.00002 : f_pip(syminfo.ticker)
float tol = float(tol_pips) * pip

// Every webhook carries the chart timeframe so the server can ignore alerts that
// were accidentally created on a non-4H chart.
f_hdr(string t) =>
    '{"secret":"' + wh_secret + '","type":"' + t + '","timeframe":"' + timeframe.period + '","exchange":"' + syminfo.prefix + '","instrument":"' + syminfo.ticker
f_num(float x) =>
    na(x) ? "null" : str.tostring(x)

// ── Daily market structure: the most recent external high / low ─────────────
// Runs on DAILY candles through request.security, so it reads the same on the
// 4H chart as on the Daily chart. Levels are body (default) or wick highs/lows
// per the "Daily levels from" setting; a break is a daily
// body CLOSE beyond a level (no tolerance). Every structure follows the same rules:
//   • first level: close above an A shape (inside a range: only after a later
//     candle traded below the A's bearish candle) → the lowest point since the A
//     is the low; mirror for V
//   • while a side is "still forming" it follows price; it is fixed once price
//     closes beyond the A/V it pulled back from
//   • close beyond the fixed high/low → new pair in that direction;
//     close beyond the opposite level → direction flips
//   • a new structure can form inside the current range at any depth; a break
//     drops every structure inside the one that broke
// Only the MOST RECENT structure is drawn (as the external high/low), and its
// most recent break — on whichever structure — is the daily breakout.

// High / low of the daily candle i bars back: body top / bottom, or wick.
f_bh(int i, bool bd) =>
    bd ? math.max(open[i], close[i]) : high[i]
f_bl(int i, bool bd) =>
    bd ? math.min(open[i], close[i]) : low[i]

f_lowest(int from_bar, bool bd) =>
    float m = f_bl(0, bd)
    int mb = bar_index
    int n = math.min(bar_index - from_bar, 1500)
    for i = 0 to n
        if f_bl(i, bd) < m
            m := f_bl(i, bd)
            mb := bar_index - i
    [m, mb]

f_highest(int from_bar, bool bd) =>
    float m = f_bh(0, bd)
    int mb = bar_index
    int n = math.min(bar_index - from_bar, 1500)
    for i = 0 to n
        if f_bh(i, bd) > m
            m := f_bh(i, bd)
            mb := bar_index - i
    [m, mb]

f_bt(int b) =>
    time[bar_index - b]

type Layer
    string dir = "none"
    float  hi = na
    int    hi_bar = na
    int    hi_t = na
    float  lo = na
    int    lo_bar = na
    int    lo_t = na
    bool   hi_fixed = false
    bool   lo_fixed = false
    float  pb_hi = na
    float  pb_lo = na

method set_hi(Layer s, float v, int b) =>
    s.hi := v
    s.hi_bar := b
    s.hi_t := f_bt(b)

method set_lo(Layer s, float v, int b) =>
    s.lo := v
    s.lo_bar := b
    s.lo_t := f_bt(b)

method reset(Layer s) =>
    s.dir := "none"
    s.hi := na
    s.lo := na
    s.hi_fixed := false
    s.lo_fixed := false
    s.pb_hi := na
    s.pb_lo := na

// One daily candle of structure logic inside [blo, bhi].
// Returns [changed, broken level, time that level formed]; changed = a break
// redefined this layer.
method step(Layer s, float blo, float bhi, float lA, int lAb, bool lAok, float lV, int lVb, bool lVok, bool bd) =>
    bool  ev   = false
    float blvl = na
    int   bt   = na
    if s.dir == "none"
        if not na(lA) and lAok and close > lA
            [m, mb] = f_lowest(lAb, bd)
            if m > blo and m < bhi
                s.dir := "bull"
                s.set_lo(m, mb)
                s.set_hi(f_bh(0, bd), bar_index)
                s.hi_fixed := false
                s.pb_lo := lV
                ev := true
                blvl := lA
                bt := f_bt(lAb)
        else if not na(lV) and lVok and close < lV
            [m, mb] = f_highest(lVb, bd)
            if m > blo and m < bhi
                s.dir := "bear"
                s.set_hi(m, mb)
                s.set_lo(f_bl(0, bd), bar_index)
                s.lo_fixed := false
                s.pb_hi := lA
                ev := true
                blvl := lV
                bt := f_bt(lVb)
    else if s.dir == "bull"
        if close < s.lo
            blvl := s.lo
            bt := s.lo_t
            s.dir := "bear"
            s.set_lo(f_bl(0, bd), bar_index)
            s.lo_fixed := false
            s.pb_hi := lA
            ev := true
        else if s.hi_fixed and close > s.hi
            blvl := s.hi
            bt := s.hi_t
            [m, mb] = f_lowest(s.hi_bar, bd)
            s.set_lo(m, mb)
            s.set_hi(f_bh(0, bd), bar_index)
            s.hi_fixed := false
            s.pb_lo := lV
            ev := true
        else
            if not s.hi_fixed and f_bh(0, bd) > s.hi
                s.set_hi(f_bh(0, bd), bar_index)
            if not s.hi_fixed and not na(s.pb_lo) and close < s.pb_lo
                s.hi_fixed := true
    else if s.dir == "bear"
        if close > s.hi
            blvl := s.hi
            bt := s.hi_t
            s.dir := "bull"
            s.set_hi(f_bh(0, bd), bar_index)
            s.hi_fixed := false
            s.pb_lo := lV
            ev := true
        else if s.lo_fixed and close < s.lo
            blvl := s.lo
            bt := s.lo_t
            [m, mb] = f_highest(s.lo_bar, bd)
            s.set_hi(m, mb)
            s.set_lo(f_bl(0, bd), bar_index)
            s.lo_fixed := false
            s.pb_hi := lA
            ev := true
        else
            if not s.lo_fixed and f_bl(0, bd) < s.lo
                s.set_lo(f_bl(0, bd), bar_index)
            if not s.lo_fixed and not na(s.pb_hi) and close > s.pb_hi
                s.lo_fixed := true
    [ev, blvl, bt]

method on_new_A(Layer s, float a) =>
    if s.dir == "bear" and not s.lo_fixed and na(s.pb_hi)
        s.pb_hi := a

method on_new_V(Layer s, float v) =>
    if s.dir == "bull" and not s.hi_fixed and na(s.pb_lo)
        s.pb_lo := v

f_structure(bool bd) =>
    // Outer structure
    var string e_dir = "none"
    var float  e_hi = na
    var int    e_hi_bar = na
    var int    e_hi_t = na
    var float  e_lo = na
    var int    e_lo_bar = na
    var int    e_lo_t = na
    var bool   e_hif = false
    var bool   e_lof = false
    var float  e_pbh = na
    var float  e_pbl = na
    // Structures inside it, outermost first; the last one is the most recent
    var array<Layer> stack = array.new<Layer>()
    // Latest unbroken A / V shapes (body or wick levels)
    var float  lastA = na
    var int    lastA_bar = na
    var float  lastA_bear_lo = na
    var bool   lastA_ok = false
    var float  lastV = na
    var int    lastV_bar = na
    var float  lastV_bull_hi = na
    var bool   lastV_ok = false
    // D.A / D.V shown on the chart (latest A / V shape)
    var float  da = na
    var int    da_t = na
    var float  dv = na
    var int    dv_t = na
    // Most recent break on any structure
    var int    b_cnt = 0
    var string b_dir = "none"
    var float  b_lvl = na
    var float  b_opp = na
    var int    b_t = na    // when the broken level formed

    bool  ext_ev = false
    float e_blvl = na
    int   e_bt = na

    // 1. Outer structure
    if e_dir == "none"
        if not na(lastA) and close > lastA
            e_blvl := lastA
            e_bt := f_bt(lastA_bar)
            [m, mb] = f_lowest(lastA_bar, bd)
            e_lo := m, e_lo_bar := mb, e_lo_t := f_bt(mb)
            e_hi := f_bh(0, bd), e_hi_bar := bar_index, e_hi_t := time
            e_dir := "bull", e_hif := false
            ext_ev := true
        else if not na(lastV) and close < lastV
            e_blvl := lastV
            e_bt := f_bt(lastV_bar)
            [m, mb] = f_highest(lastV_bar, bd)
            e_hi := m, e_hi_bar := mb, e_hi_t := f_bt(mb)
            e_lo := f_bl(0, bd), e_lo_bar := bar_index, e_lo_t := time
            e_dir := "bear", e_lof := false
            ext_ev := true
    else if e_dir == "bull"
        if close < e_lo
            e_blvl := e_lo
            e_bt := e_lo_t
            e_dir := "bear"
            e_lo := f_bl(0, bd), e_lo_bar := bar_index, e_lo_t := time
            e_lof := false
            ext_ev := true
        else if e_hif and close > e_hi
            e_blvl := e_hi
            e_bt := e_hi_t
            [m, mb] = f_lowest(e_hi_bar, bd)
            e_lo := m, e_lo_bar := mb, e_lo_t := f_bt(mb)
            e_hi := f_bh(0, bd), e_hi_bar := bar_index, e_hi_t := time
            e_hif := false
            ext_ev := true
        else
            if not e_hif and f_bh(0, bd) > e_hi
                e_hi := f_bh(0, bd), e_hi_bar := bar_index, e_hi_t := time
            if not e_hif and not na(e_pbl) and close < e_pbl
                e_hif := true
    else if e_dir == "bear"
        if close > e_hi
            e_blvl := e_hi
            e_bt := e_hi_t
            e_dir := "bull"
            e_hi := f_bh(0, bd), e_hi_bar := bar_index, e_hi_t := time
            e_hif := false
            ext_ev := true
        else if e_lof and close < e_lo
            e_blvl := e_lo
            e_bt := e_lo_t
            [m, mb] = f_highest(e_lo_bar, bd)
            e_hi := m, e_hi_bar := mb, e_hi_t := f_bt(mb)
            e_lo := f_bl(0, bd), e_lo_bar := bar_index, e_lo_t := time
            e_lof := false
            ext_ev := true
        else
            if not e_lof and f_bl(0, bd) < e_lo
                e_lo := f_bl(0, bd), e_lo_bar := bar_index, e_lo_t := time
            if not e_lof and not na(e_pbh) and close > e_pbh
                e_lof := true

    if ext_ev
        e_pbh := na, e_pbl := na
        array.clear(stack)
        b_cnt += 1
        b_dir := e_dir == "bull" ? "bullish" : "bearish"
        b_lvl := e_blvl
        b_t   := e_bt
        b_opp := e_dir == "bull" ? e_lo : e_hi

    // 2. Structures inside it, from the outside in. A break drops everything
    //    inside the structure that broke; if nothing broke, look for a new
    //    structure inside the most recent range.
    if not na(lastA) and not lastA_ok and f_bl(0, bd) < lastA_bear_lo
        lastA_ok := true
    if not na(lastV) and not lastV_ok and f_bh(0, bd) > lastV_bull_hi
        lastV_ok := true

    if not ext_ev and e_dir != "none"
        float blo = e_lo
        float bhi = e_hi
        bool broke = false
        int n = array.size(stack)
        if n > 0
            for k = 0 to n - 1
                Layer L = array.get(stack, k)
                [ev, lvl, lt] = L.step(blo, bhi, lastA, lastA_bar, lastA_ok, lastV, lastV_bar, lastV_ok, bd)
                if ev
                    while array.size(stack) > k + 1
                        array.pop(stack)
                    broke := true
                    b_cnt += 1
                    b_dir := L.dir == "bull" ? "bullish" : "bearish"
                    b_lvl := lvl
                    b_t   := lt
                    b_opp := L.dir == "bull" ? L.lo : L.hi
                    break
                blo := L.lo
                bhi := L.hi
        if not broke and array.size(stack) < 30
            Layer nl = Layer.new()
            [nev, nlvl, nlt] = nl.step(blo, bhi, lastA, lastA_bar, lastA_ok, lastV, lastV_bar, lastV_ok, bd)
            if nev
                array.push(stack, nl)
                b_cnt += 1
                b_dir := nl.dir == "bull" ? "bullish" : "bearish"
                b_lvl := nlvl
                b_t   := nlt
                b_opp := nl.dir == "bull" ? nl.lo : nl.hi

    // Clear broken shapes / outer pullback triggers
    if not na(lastA) and close > lastA
        lastA := na
    if not na(lastV) and close < lastV
        lastV := na
    if not na(e_pbh) and close > e_pbh
        e_pbh := na
    if not na(e_pbl) and close < e_pbl
        e_pbl := na

    // 3. Register new A / V shapes
    bool isA = close[1] > open[1] and close < open
    bool isV = close[1] < open[1] and close > open
    if isA
        lastA := math.max(f_bh(0, bd), f_bh(1, bd))
        lastA_bar := f_bh(0, bd) >= f_bh(1, bd) ? bar_index : bar_index - 1
        lastA_bear_lo := f_bl(0, bd)
        lastA_ok := false
        da := lastA, da_t := f_bt(lastA_bar)
        if e_dir != "none"
            e_pbh := lastA
        for L in stack
            L.on_new_A(lastA)
    if isV
        lastV := math.min(f_bl(0, bd), f_bl(1, bd))
        lastV_bar := f_bl(0, bd) <= f_bl(1, bd) ? bar_index : bar_index - 1
        lastV_bull_hi := f_bh(0, bd)
        lastV_ok := false
        dv := lastV, dv_t := f_bt(lastV_bar)
        if e_dir != "none"
            e_pbl := lastV
        for L in stack
            L.on_new_V(lastV)

    // 4. The most recent structure (what the chart shows as External high / low)
    string c_dir = e_dir
    float  c_hi  = e_hi
    float  c_lo  = e_lo
    bool   c_hif = e_hif
    bool   c_lof = e_lof
    int    c_hit = e_hi_t
    int    c_lot = e_lo_t
    if array.size(stack) > 0
        Layer cur = array.last(stack)
        c_dir := cur.dir
        c_hi  := cur.hi
        c_lo  := cur.lo
        c_hif := cur.hi_fixed
        c_lof := cur.lo_fixed
        c_hit := cur.hi_t
        c_lot := cur.lo_t
    // [1] + lookahead_on = state after the last COMPLETED daily candle (no repaint)
    [c_dir[1], c_hi[1], c_lo[1], c_hif[1], c_lof[1], c_hit[1], c_lot[1],
     b_cnt[1], b_dir[1], b_lvl[1], b_opp[1],
     da[1], da_t[1], dv[1], dv_t[1], b_t[1]]

[s_cdir, s_chi, s_clo, s_chif, s_clof, s_chit, s_clot,
 s_bcnt, s_bdir, s_blvl, s_bopp,
 s_da, s_da_t, s_dv, s_dv_t, s_bt] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_structure(d_body), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// The same structure engine on WEEKLY candles (Weekly External high / low)
[w_cdir, w_chi, w_clo, w_chif, w_clof, w_chit, w_clot,
 w_bcnt, w_bdir, w_blvl, w_bopp,
 w_da, w_da_t, w_dv, w_dv_t, w_bt] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", f_structure(w_body), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
// Last two completed Weekly candles (levels per the Body/Wick setting), and the
// wicks of the 1st and 3rd of the last three (Weekly FVGs): one request
[wk_o1, wk_c1, wk_h1, wk_l1, wk_o2, wk_c2, wk_h2, wk_l2, wg_h1, wg_l1, wg_h3, wg_l3] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W",
     [open[1], close[1], f_bh(1, w_body), f_bl(1, w_body), open[2], close[2], f_bh(2, w_body), f_bl(2, w_body), high[1], low[1], high[3], low[3]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ── Daily OHLC (for post-breakout OCs) ────────────────────────────────────────
// lookahead_on + [1] = the just-completed daily candle on every H4 bar of the
// next day, on history and live (non-repainting).
// Last completed Daily candle as drawn (wicks), for the server's chart pictures
// One request for every Daily value below: the last completed candle (wicks, and
// body/wick levels per "Daily levels from"), the one before it, and the 3rd back
[dr_t, dr_o, dr_h, dr_l, dr_c, d_high, d_low, d_open2, d_close2, d_high2, d_low2, dw_h2, dw_l2, dw_t2, dg_h3, dg_l3] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D",
     [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], f_bh(1, d_body), f_bl(1, d_body), open[2], close[2], f_bh(2, d_body), f_bl(2, d_body), high[2], low[2], time[2], high[3], low[3]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
const int HIST_N = 40
var array<int>   dh_t = array.new<int>()
var array<float> dh_o = array.new<float>()
var array<float> dh_h = array.new<float>()
var array<float> dh_l = array.new<float>()
var array<float> dh_c = array.new<float>()
if timeframe.change("D") and not na(dr_t)
    array.push(dh_t, dr_t)
    array.push(dh_o, dr_o)
    array.push(dh_h, dr_h)
    array.push(dh_l, dr_l)
    array.push(dh_c, dr_c)
    if array.size(dh_t) > HIST_N
        array.shift(dh_t)
        array.shift(dh_o)
        array.shift(dh_h)
        array.shift(dh_l)
        array.shift(dh_c)
f_bar(int t, float o, float h, float l, float c) =>
    na(t) or na(c) ? "null" : '[' + str.tostring(t) + ',' + str.tostring(o, format.mintick) + ',' + str.tostring(h, format.mintick) + ',' + str.tostring(l, format.mintick) + ',' + str.tostring(c, format.mintick) + ']'

// Last completed Daily candle's open / close; Daily FVGs use the wicks of the 1st
// (dg_h1 / dg_l1) and 3rd (dg_h3 / dg_l3) of the last three completed candles;
// dw_h2 / dw_l2 = the wicks of the candle before the last one (Daily engulfing)
float d_open  = dr_o
float d_close = dr_c
float dg_h1   = dr_h
float dg_l1   = dr_l

f_layer_name(string l) =>
    l == "external" ? "External" : l == "internal" ? "Internal" : l == "inner_internal" ? "Inner internal" : l == "sub_internal" ? "Sub-internal" : ""

// ── Persistent state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string bo_dir     = na
// How this Daily setup relates to the Weekly: "confirmed" (the Daily broke in the
// Weekly direction while a Weekly reaction held), "inline", "against" or "".
var string bo_wk_rel     = ""
var string bo_wk_dir     = na
var float  bo_wk_lvl     = na
var string bo_wk_src     = na
var float  bo_wk_src_lvl = na
var string bo_wk_cls     = na
var float  bo_level   = na
var string bo_layer   = na   // which level broke: external | internal | inner_internal | sub_internal
var float  bo_opp     = na   // other side of the range that was just broken
var int    last_bcnt  = 0
var bool   est_above  = false
var bool   est_below  = false
var bool   retest_on  = false
var string retest_src = na
var string retest_kind = na   // inside-range reactions: "v_shape" | "a_shape" | "oc"
// Every Daily V-/A-shape (wick level) and Daily OC. An inside-range reaction must
// come from one of these whose level sits inside the range that was just broken.
var array<float> d_vs   = array.new<float>()   // V-shapes  (buy reactions)
var array<float> d_as   = array.new<float>()   // A-shapes  (sell reactions)
var array<float> d_boc  = array.new<float>()   // bullish OCs (buy reactions)
var array<float> d_soc  = array.new<float>()   // bearish OCs (sell reactions)
var float  h4_a_lvl   = na
var float  h4_v_lvl   = na
var int    pb_consec  = 0
var float  pb_close1  = na
var float  pb_oc_lvl  = na   // most recent post-breakout OC (for the label)
var array<float> pb_ocs = array.new<float>()   // every completed post-breakout OC
var float  retest_lvl = na   // level of the zone price is currently reacting from
var float  retest_lvl2 = na  // Daily FVG reactions: the far edge of the gap (retest_lvl = the near edge)
// Daily FVGs (gap top / bottom). Bullish = buy reaction zones, bearish = sell.
var array<float> d_bf_hi = array.new<float>()
var array<float> d_bf_lo = array.new<float>()
var array<float> d_sf_hi = array.new<float>()
var array<float> d_sf_lo = array.new<float>()
// Each FVG's own External H4 level (A for bullish gaps, V for bearish) and the bar
// it was set on: from the candle that first entered it, moved by each deeper
// Daily candle while it is the reaction. Kept so a return to the same FVG (or a
// deeper FVG taking over) uses that FVG's own level.
var array<float> d_bf_x  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   d_bf_xb = array.new<int>()
var array<float> d_sf_x  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   d_sf_xb = array.new<int>()
// Pierced: price has traded beyond the gap's far edge (below a bullish gap, above
// a bearish one). A bullish FVG only reacts when price dips INTO it from above,
// so once pierced it can't start a new reaction (coming back up into it from
// below doesn't count). A reaction already running there is not ended by this.
var array<bool>  d_bf_p  = array.new<bool>()
var array<bool>  d_sf_p  = array.new<bool>()
// Used Daily levels: a Daily level (Breaker, OC, V/A-shape) that has given its
// H4 confirmation never starts a reaction again; a used Daily FVG is removed.
var array<float> d_used = array.new<float>()
// H4 FVG after an H4 breakout in line with the Daily: checked on the next candle
var int    h4f_bar  = na
var bool   h4f_bull = false
var float  h4f_ref  = na   // high (buys) / low (sells) of the candle before the breakout
// Daily FVG reactions: today's first H4 entry into the gap, and the H4 A / V then
var int    fz_day_bar  = na
var float  fz_day_a    = na
var float  fz_day_v    = na
var bool   fz_day_done = false
var int    retest_bar = na   // bar the current reaction started on
// External/Internal is judged from the FIRST reaction at the daily level that
// confirms: a failed reaction that restarts at the same level keeps that start;
// a reaction at a different daily level starts fresh from that level.
var float  anchor_lvl = na
var int    anchor_bar = na
var bool   just_broke = false

// ── H4 continuation state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var bool   h4_bo_fired           = false
var bool   h4_breaker_orig_fired = false
var float  h4_breaker_lvl        = na
var float  h4_invalid_lvl        = na
var bool   h4_aligned            = false
// H4 OCs for trend continuation: every OC in the daily direction, each with the
// bar it formed on (its second candle). At each H4 breakout in the daily
// direction only that breakout's leg (from its swing low/high) is kept; each OC
// alerts once then is removed; all go when H4 breaks the other way.
var array<float> h4_ocs = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   h4_ocb = array.new<int>()
var float  h4_brk_lvl = na   // H4 A (buy) / V (sell) level last broken in the daily direction

// Continuation dedup: each level fires at most once per "visit". It re-arms
// when a new level is set (level-change) OR when price leaves the zone, so a
// second identical alert cannot fire on the next H4 candle while price just
// sits at the level.
var bool   bk_armed              = true
var float  bk_armed_lvl          = na

// ── Level origin bar tracking (for extend-right lines) ───────────────────────
var int    poc_origin = na
var int    h4a_origin = na
var int    h4v_origin = na
var int    bk_origin  = na
var int    h4c_origin = na

// ── Daily breakout: the most recent break on any structure layer ─────────────
bool new_daily = timeframe.change("D")
if new_daily
    just_broke := false

// ── Weekly storyline: Weekly breakout → Weekly reaction → Daily breakout ─────
// The Daily rules one level up (v10): Weekly candles set the Weekly direction,
// DAILY candles react at Weekly levels, and a Daily breakout in the Weekly
// direction plays the part the H4 breakout plays for the Daily.
//   • A Weekly close beyond the Weekly External high/low is a Weekly breakout;
//     its own close beyond the Breaker (± allowance) counts as moving away.
//   • Weekly reaction levels: post-breakout Weekly OCs, Weekly V-shapes (A for
//     sells) formed after the breakout, Weekly FVGs after the breakout, the
//     Weekly Breaker, Weekly V/A-shapes and OCs inside the broken Weekly range,
//     Weekly FVGs inside that range. Exact Daily wick touch that holds.
//   • External / Internal: the FIRST Daily touch of a Weekly level after it
//     formed is the start; the Daily level that breaks is External if it formed
//     before that, Internal if after. With Internal off, an Internal break
//     doesn't use up the Weekly reaction (the Daily setup is then "in line").
//   • Weekly FVGs: react only when a Daily candle dips into the gap from above
//     (rises into it from below, sells); only a Weekly close through the gap
//     kills it; each Weekly candle that dips below the previous Weekly low inside
//     it restarts the check; a deeper FVG takes over; each FVG keeps its own
//     start; a Weekly-confirmed Daily breakout from one uses up those above it.
//   • A Weekly-confirmed Daily breakout uses up that Weekly reaction; a Weekly
//     breakout the same way keeps going, the other way resets.
// The Weekly never fires an alert itself: it labels the Daily setup
// (Weekly-confirmed External / Internal, in line, or AGAINST).
var string wk_dir      = na
var float  wk_level    = na
var float  wk_opp      = na
var int    last_wcnt   = 0
var bool   wk_est      = false
var bool   wk_react    = false
var string wk_src      = na
var string wk_kind     = na
var float  wk_src_lvl  = na
var float  wk_src_lvl2 = na   // Weekly FVG reactions: the far edge of the gap
var float  wk_anchor_lvl = na
var int    wk_anchor_t = na   // when the reacting Weekly level was first touched (its External start)
var bool   wk_just_broke = false
var array<float> w_vs   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_as   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_boc  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_soc  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_pbocs = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_seen = array.new<float>()   // Weekly levels already touched by a Daily candle
// Used Weekly levels: one that gave a Weekly-confirmed Daily breakout, or whose
// reaction failed, never starts another Weekly reaction (a used Weekly FVG is removed)
var array<float> w_used = array.new<float>()
// Weekly FVGs: gap top / bottom, own External start (time), pierced
var array<float> w_bf_hi = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_bf_lo = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   w_bf_x  = array.new<int>()
var array<bool>  w_bf_p  = array.new<bool>()
var array<float> w_sf_hi = array.new<float>()
var array<float> w_sf_lo = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   w_sf_x  = array.new<int>()
var array<bool>  w_sf_p  = array.new<bool>()
var int    wfz_t    = na      // this week's first Daily entry into the reacting Weekly FVG
var bool   wfz_done = false
var int    wpb_consec  = 0
var float  wpb_close1  = na
var float  wpb_oc_lvl  = na

bool new_week = timeframe.change("W")
if new_week
    wk_just_broke := false

if not na(w_bcnt) and w_bcnt > 0 and w_bcnt != last_wcnt
    last_wcnt   := w_bcnt
    wk_dir      := w_bdir
    wk_level    := w_blvl
    wk_opp      := w_bopp
    // the breakout Week's own close beyond the Breaker counts as moving away
    wk_est      := not na(wk_c1) and (w_bdir == "bullish" ? wk_c1 > w_blvl + tol : wk_c1 < w_blvl - tol)
    wk_react    := false
    wk_src      := na
    wk_kind     := na
    wk_src_lvl  := na
    wk_src_lvl2 := na
    wk_anchor_lvl := na
    wk_anchor_t := na
    wpb_consec  := 0
    wpb_close1  := na
    wpb_oc_lvl  := na
    array.clear(w_pbocs)
    wk_just_broke := true

f_wkeep(array<float> a, float v) =>
    array.push(a, v)
    if array.size(a) > 120
        array.shift(a)

f_wkill(array<float> a, float c, bool buy_lvl) =>
    int k = array.size(a) - 1
    while k >= 0
        float L = array.get(a, k)
        if buy_lvl ? c < L : c > L
            array.remove(a, k)
        k -= 1

f_wfdrop(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<int> xs, array<bool> ps, int k) =>
    array.remove(his, k)
    array.remove(los, k)
    array.remove(xs, k)
    array.remove(ps, k)
f_wfkeep(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<int> xs, array<bool> ps, float h, float l) =>
    array.push(his, h)
    array.push(los, l)
    array.push(xs, na)
    array.push(ps, false)
    if array.size(his) > 40
        f_wfdrop(his, los, xs, ps, 0)
f_wfkill(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<int> xs, array<bool> ps, float c, bool bull) =>
    int k = array.size(his) - 1
    while k >= 0
        if bull ? c < array.get(los, k) : c > array.get(his, k)
            f_wfdrop(his, los, xs, ps, k)
        k -= 1
f_wseen(float L) =>
    bool found = false
    for x in w_seen
        if math.abs(x - L) <= pip * 0.1
            found := true
    found

f_wused(float L) =>
    bool found = false
    for x in w_used
        if math.abs(x - L) <= pip * 0.1
            found := true
    found

// Deepest level in lv that the Daily candle (lo_, hi_, cl_) touches exactly and holds
f_wpick(array<float> lv, bool bull, float lo_lim, float hi_lim, float t, float lo_, float hi_, float cl_) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(lv) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lv) - 1
            float L = array.get(lv, i)
            bool inside = L > lo_lim and L < hi_lim
            bool touched = lo_ <= L and hi_ >= L
            bool held = bull ? cl_ >= L - t : cl_ <= L + t
            if inside and touched and held and not f_wused(L) and (na(best) or (bull ? L < best : L > best))
                best := L
    best

// Deepest Weekly FVG the Daily candle (lo_, hi_) enters, not pierced. inside: the
// whole gap inside the broken Weekly range; otherwise reaching beyond the Breaker.
f_wfpick(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<bool> ps, bool bull, bool inside, float opp, float b_lo, float b_hi, float lo_, float hi_) =>
    int   best = -1
    float bv   = na
    if array.size(his) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(his) - 1
            float H = array.get(his, i)
            float L = array.get(los, i)
            bool in_pos  = inside ? (not na(opp) and (bull ? (L > opp and H < b_lo) : (H < opp and L > b_hi))) : (bull ? H > b_hi : L < b_lo)
            float edge   = bull ? L : H
            if in_pos and lo_ <= H and hi_ >= L and not array.get(ps, i) and (na(bv) or (bull ? edge < bv : edge > bv))
                bv   := edge
                best := i
    best

// Weekly reaction, checked on each completed Daily candle (before this week's
// new levels are added, so the candles that formed a level can't react to it)
if new_daily and not na(wk_dir) and not na(wk_level) and not na(d_close) and not na(dr_h)
    bool wb = wk_dir == "bullish"
    bool w_was_est = wk_est
    if wb ? d_close > wk_level + tol : d_close < wk_level - tol
        wk_est := true
    array<float> wfh = wb ? w_bf_hi : w_sf_hi
    array<float> wfl = wb ? w_bf_lo : w_sf_lo
    array<int>   wfx = wb ? w_bf_x  : w_sf_x
    array<bool>  wfp = wb ? w_bf_p  : w_sf_p
    float wb_lo = wk_level - tol
    float wb_hi = wk_level + tol

    // First Daily touch of each Weekly level since it formed: the External start
    bool w_first = false
    array<float> wcand = array.new<float>()
    array.push(wcand, wk_level)
    for L in w_pbocs
        array.push(wcand, L)
    array<float> wshp = wb ? w_vs : w_as
    array<float> wocl = wb ? w_boc : w_soc
    for L in wshp
        array.push(wcand, L)
    for L in wocl
        array.push(wcand, L)
    for L in wcand
        bool w_held = wb ? d_close >= L - tol : d_close <= L + tol
        if dr_l <= L and dr_h >= L and w_held and not f_wseen(L)
            array.push(w_seen, L)
            w_first := true
    if array.size(wfh) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(wfh) - 1
            float gH = array.get(wfh, i)
            float gL = array.get(wfl, i)
            float gK = wb ? gH : gL
            if dr_l <= gH and dr_h >= gL and not array.get(wfp, i) and not f_wseen(gK)
                array.push(w_seen, gK)
                array.set(wfx, i, dr_t)
                w_first := true
    if array.size(w_seen) > 300
        array.shift(w_seen)
    if w_first
        wk_anchor_t := dr_t

    // A reaction fails on a Daily close back through its level (a Weekly FVG only
    // on a Weekly close through the gap, checked when the week closes)
    bool w_fvg = wk_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or wk_src == "inside_fvg"
    if wk_react and not w_fvg
        if wb ? d_close < wk_src_lvl - tol : d_close > wk_src_lvl + tol
            array.push(w_used, wk_src_lvl)   // a failed reaction uses the level too
            wk_react   := false
            wk_src     := na
            wk_kind    := na
            wk_src_lvl := na
            wk_src_lvl2 := na

    if not wk_react and w_was_est
        // post-breakout OCs, V/A after the breakout, FVGs after the breakout, the
        // Breaker, then inside the range (V/A, OC, FVG)
        float pbw = f_wpick(w_pbocs, wb, wb ? wb_hi : -1e18, wb ? 1e18 : wb_lo, tol, dr_l, dr_h, d_close)
        float pvw = f_wpick(wb ? w_vs : w_as, wb, wb ? wb_hi : -1e18, wb ? 1e18 : wb_lo, tol, dr_l, dr_h, d_close)
        int   pfw = f_wfpick(wfh, wfl, wfp, wb, false, wk_opp, wb_lo, wb_hi, dr_l, dr_h)
        bool  bkw = dr_l <= wk_level and dr_h >= wk_level and (wb ? d_close >= wb_lo : d_close <= wb_hi) and not f_wused(wk_level)
        float ir_lo = wb ? wk_opp : wb_hi
        float ir_hi = wb ? wb_lo : wk_opp
        float shw = na(wk_opp) ? na : f_wpick(wb ? w_vs : w_as, wb, ir_lo, ir_hi, tol, dr_l, dr_h, d_close)
        float ocw = na(wk_opp) ? na : f_wpick(wb ? w_boc : w_soc, wb, ir_lo, ir_hi, tol, dr_l, dr_h, d_close)
        int   ifw = f_wfpick(wfh, wfl, wfp, wb, true, wk_opp, wb_lo, wb_hi, dr_l, dr_h)
        float hit = na
        float hit2 = na
        string hsrc = na
        string hkind = na
        int   hfi = -1
        if not na(pbw)
            hit := pbw, hsrc := "post_breakout_oc"
        else if not na(pvw)
            hit := pvw, hsrc := "post_breakout_v"
        else if pfw >= 0
            hfi := pfw, hsrc := "post_breakout_fvg"
        else if bkw
            hit := wk_level, hsrc := "breaker"
        else
            if not na(shw)
                hit := shw, hsrc := "inside_range", hkind := wb ? "v_shape" : "a_shape"
            if not na(ocw) and (na(hit) or (wb ? ocw < hit : ocw > hit))
                hit := ocw, hsrc := "inside_range", hkind := "oc"
            if na(hit) and ifw >= 0
                hfi := ifw, hsrc := "inside_fvg"
        if hfi >= 0
            hit  := wb ? array.get(wfh, hfi) : array.get(wfl, hfi)
            hit2 := wb ? array.get(wfl, hfi) : array.get(wfh, hfi)
        if not na(hit)
            wk_react    := true
            wk_src      := hsrc
            wk_kind     := hkind
            wk_src_lvl  := hit
            wk_src_lvl2 := hit2
            wfz_t       := na
            wfz_done    := false
            wk_anchor_lvl := hit
            if hfi >= 0 and not na(array.get(wfx, hfi))
                wk_anchor_t := array.get(wfx, hfi)   // the FVG's own start
            else if na(wk_anchor_t)
                wk_anchor_t := dr_t

    // Weekly FVG reactions: a deeper FVG takes over, and each Weekly candle that
    // dips below the previous Weekly low inside the gap restarts the check
    if wk_react and (wk_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or wk_src == "inside_fvg")
        float cur_hi = math.max(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
        float cur_lo = math.min(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
        int dk = -1
        if array.size(wfh) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(wfh) - 1
                float gH = array.get(wfh, i)
                float gL = array.get(wfl, i)
                bool deeper = wb ? gH < cur_lo : gL > cur_hi
                bool ok_pos = wb ? (gH > wb_hi or (not na(wk_opp) and gL > wk_opp and gH < wb_lo)) : (gL < wb_lo or (not na(wk_opp) and gH < wk_opp and gL > wb_hi))
                if deeper and ok_pos and not array.get(wfp, i) and dr_l <= gH and dr_h >= gL and (dk < 0 or (wb ? gL < array.get(wfl, dk) : gH > array.get(wfh, dk)))
                    dk := i
        if dk >= 0
            float dH = array.get(wfh, dk)
            float dL = array.get(wfl, dk)
            wk_src      := (wb ? dH > wb_hi : dL < wb_lo) ? "post_breakout_fvg" : "inside_fvg"
            wk_src_lvl  := wb ? dH : dL
            wk_src_lvl2 := wb ? dL : dH
            wk_anchor_lvl := wk_src_lvl
            wk_anchor_t := na(array.get(wfx, dk)) ? dr_t : array.get(wfx, dk)
            wfz_t       := na
            wfz_done    := false
        float ah = math.max(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
        float al = math.min(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
        if na(wfz_t) and dr_l <= ah and dr_h >= al
            wfz_t := dr_t
        if not wfz_done and not na(wfz_t) and not na(wg_l1) and (wb ? dr_l < wg_l1 : dr_h > wg_h1)
            wfz_done    := true
            wk_anchor_t := wfz_t
            if array.size(wfh) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(wfh) - 1
                    if math.abs(array.get(wfh, i) - ah) <= pip * 0.1 and math.abs(array.get(wfl, i) - al) <= pip * 0.1
                        array.set(wfx, i, wfz_t)

    // Pierced Weekly FVGs (after this Daily candle's checks): traded past the far edge
    if array.size(w_bf_lo) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(w_bf_lo) - 1
            if dr_l < array.get(w_bf_lo, i)
                array.set(w_bf_p, i, true)
    if array.size(w_sf_hi) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(w_sf_hi) - 1
            if dr_h > array.get(w_sf_hi, i)
                array.set(w_sf_p, i, true)

// Weekly V/A-shapes and OCs (a Weekly close through one kills it), the
// post-breakout Weekly OCs, and Weekly FVGs (only a Weekly close through the gap
// kills one, and ends a reaction at it)
if new_week and not na(wk_c1)
    f_wkill(w_vs,  wk_c1, true)
    f_wkill(w_boc, wk_c1, true)
    f_wkill(w_as,  wk_c1, false)
    f_wkill(w_soc, wk_c1, false)
    f_wfkill(w_bf_hi, w_bf_lo, w_bf_x, w_bf_p, wk_c1, true)
    f_wfkill(w_sf_hi, w_sf_lo, w_sf_x, w_sf_p, wk_c1, false)
    if wk_react and (wk_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or wk_src == "inside_fvg") and (wk_dir == "bullish" ? wk_c1 < wk_src_lvl2 : wk_c1 > wk_src_lvl2)
        wk_react    := false
        wk_src      := na
        wk_kind     := na
        wk_src_lvl  := na
        wk_src_lvl2 := na
    wfz_t    := na
    wfz_done := false
    if not na(wg_h3) and not na(wg_l1)
        if wg_l1 > wg_h3
            f_wfkeep(w_bf_hi, w_bf_lo, w_bf_x, w_bf_p, wg_l1, wg_h3)
        if wg_h1 < wg_l3
            f_wfkeep(w_sf_hi, w_sf_lo, w_sf_x, w_sf_p, wg_l3, wg_h1)
    if not na(wk_dir)
        f_wkill(w_pbocs, wk_c1, wk_dir == "bullish")
        wpb_oc_lvl := array.size(w_pbocs) > 0 ? array.last(w_pbocs) : na
    if not na(wk_c2)
        bool wy_bull = wk_c1 > wk_o1
        bool wy_bear = wk_c1 < wk_o1
        bool wp_bull = wk_c2 > wk_o2
        bool wp_bear = wk_c2 < wk_o2
        if wp_bear and wy_bull
            f_wkeep(w_vs, math.min(wk_l2, wk_l1))
        if wp_bull and wy_bear
            f_wkeep(w_as, math.max(wk_h2, wk_h1))
        if wp_bull and wy_bull
            f_wkeep(w_boc, wk_c2)
        if wp_bear and wy_bear
            f_wkeep(w_soc, wk_c2)
    if not na(wk_dir) and not wk_just_broke
        bool wmatch = wk_dir == "bullish" ? (wk_c1 >= wk_o1 and wk_c1 > wk_level) : (wk_c1 < wk_o1 and wk_c1 < wk_level)
        if wmatch
            wpb_consec := wpb_consec + 1
            if wpb_consec == 1
                wpb_close1 := wk_c1
            else
                wpb_oc_lvl := wpb_close1
                array.push(w_pbocs, wpb_close1)
                if array.size(w_pbocs) > 30
                    array.shift(w_pbocs)
                wpb_close1 := wk_c1
        else
            wpb_consec := 0

f_wsrc_name(string src, string kind) =>
    src == "breaker" ? "Weekly Breaker" : src == "post_breakout_oc" ? "post-breakout Weekly OC" : src == "post_breakout_v" ? "Weekly V/A-shape after the breakout" : src == "post_breakout_fvg" ? "Weekly FVG after the breakout" : src == "inside_fvg" ? "Weekly FVG inside the range" : kind == "oc" ? "Weekly OC inside the range" : kind == "a_shape" ? "Weekly A-shape inside the range" : "Weekly V-shape inside the range"

// The reacting level as text: a Daily FVG shows its gap (bottom – top)
f_bt_lvtxt(float v) =>
    na(retest_lvl2) ? str.tostring(v, format.mintick) : str.tostring(math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2), format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2), format.mintick)

f_bt_src(string s) =>
    s == "daily_breaker" ? "Daily Breaker" : s == "post_breakout_oc" ? "Daily OC after the breakout" : s == "post_breakout_v" ? "Daily V/A-shape after the breakout" : s == "inside_range" ? "Daily level inside the broken range" : s == "post_breakout_fvg" ? "Daily FVG after the breakout" : s == "inside_fvg" ? "Daily FVG inside the range" : "-"

// The small mark on the candle that triggered a confirmation alert (engulfing and H4 FVG
// alerts get a dot instead, kept apart from the confirmations)
f_mark(bool bull) =>
    bt_mark_shape == "Dot" ? "•" : bull ? "▲" : "▼"

// Backtest: label where an alert is sent (returns true if labelled)
f_btlbl(bool bull, int kind, string cls, float h4lvl, float dlvl, string note) =>
    bool conf = kind <= 1 or kind == 7   // an H4 confirmation after a Daily reaction
    bool tf_ok = timeframe.period == "240" and bt_show   // the H4 steps only mean something on 4H candles
    bool on = kind == 11 ? bt_dengulf : kind == 10 ? bt_h4fvg : kind == 7 ? bt_react : kind == 0 ? bt_origin : kind == 1 ? bt_realign : kind == 2 ? bt_inline : kind <= 4 ? bt_breaker : kind == 5 ? bt_oc : bt_engulf
    if conf
        array.set(bt_scls, 0, cls)
    string c = array.get(bt_scls, 0)
    bool cls_ok = c == "" or kind >= 10 or (c == "external" ? bt_ext : bt_int)   // H4 FVG / Daily engulfing: no H4 class
    // H4 FVG: no buy / sell, just the pair and the message (for tracking liquidity)
    string head = kind == 10 ? syminfo.ticker + "\nH4 FVG candle after breakout has formed" : kind == 11 ? syminfo.ticker + "\nDaily " + (bull ? "buy" : "sell") + " engulfing candle has formed" : kind == 0 ? (bull ? "BUY CONFIRMED" : "SELL CONFIRMED") : (bull ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " · " + array.get(BT_NAMES, kind)
    string tag  = c == "" or kind >= 10 ? "" : conf ? (c == "external" ? " (External)" : " (Internal)") : (c == "external" ? " (External setup)" : " (Internal setup)")
    string detail = array.get(BT_NAMES, kind) + " @ " + str.tostring(h4lvl, format.mintick)
         + (note == "" ? "" : "\n" + note) + "\nDaily breakout @ " + str.tostring(dlvl, format.mintick)
         + "\nConfirmed at this candle's close: " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
         + "\nEntry = next candle's open"
    bool circles = bt_marks == "Circle + info table"
    // Kept apart from the confirmation alerts so they never replace the latest
    // confirmation arrow: the H4 FVG gets its own dot and table row; an engulfing
    // (H4 / Daily) is drawn as a box with a D / H4 pointer by the caller (f_eng_draw)
    bool eng = kind == 6 or kind == 11
    int  sl = kind == 10 ? 1 : 0
    string mk = sl == 1 ? "•" : f_mark(bull)
    if tf_ok and bt_grey and not eng and not (on and cls_ok and time >= bt_from)
        string why = time < bt_from ? "before the backtest start" : not cls_ok ? "Internal is switched off" : "this type is switched off"
        string gtxt = "Not counted: " + why + "\n" + head + tag + (conf and bt_swtxt != "" ? "\n" + bt_swtxt : "")
        if bt_latest
            label.delete(array.get(bt_last, sl))
        label glb = na
        if circles
            glb := label.new(bar_index, bull ? low : high, mk, yloc=bull ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar, style=label.style_none, textcolor=bt_grey_col, size=size.small, tooltip=gtxt + "\n" + detail)
        else
            glb := label.new(bar_index, bull ? low : high, gtxt, style=bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=bt_grey_col,
                 textcolor=bt_txt_col, size=size.small)
        array.set(bt_last, sl, glb)
        array.set(bt_info, sl * 2, gtxt + "\n" + detail)
        array.set(bt_info, sl * 2 + 1, str.format_time(time, "dd MMM yyyy HH:mm"))
    if tf_ok and on and cls_ok and time >= bt_from
        if not eng
            string atxt = (kind >= 10 ? "" : "H4 aligned - Alert\n") + head + tag + (bt_weekly and bo_wk_rel == "against" ? "\nWeekly AGAINST" : "") + (conf and bt_swtxt != "" ? "\n" + bt_swtxt : "")
            color  acol = kind >= 10 ? bt_h4fvg_col : bull ? bt_buy_col : bt_sell_col   // markers: no buy / sell colour
            if bt_latest
                label.delete(array.get(bt_last, sl))
            label alb = na
            if circles
                alb := label.new(bar_index, bull ? low : high, mk, yloc=bull ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar, style=label.style_none, textcolor=acol, size=size.small, tooltip=atxt + "\n" + detail)
            else
                alb := label.new(bar_index, bull ? low : high, atxt, style=bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=acol,
                     textcolor=bt_txt_col, size=kind == 0 ? size.normal : size.small, tooltip=detail)
            array.set(bt_last, sl, alb)
            array.set(bt_info, sl * 2, atxt + "\n" + detail)
            array.set(bt_info, sl * 2 + 1, str.format_time(time, "dd MMM yyyy HH:mm"))
        array.set(bt_cnt, kind, array.get(bt_cnt, kind) + 1)
        array.set(bt_cnt, bull ? 8 : 9, array.get(bt_cnt, bull ? 8 : 9) + 1)
    tf_ok and on and cls_ok and time >= bt_from

// Engulfing on the chart: a box over the two candles and a pointer under it, "D"
// (Daily) or "H4", each in its own colour. Only the last eng_n_d / eng_n_h stay.
// Times are bar open times.
f_eng_draw(bool daily, int t1, int t2, float top, float bot, string tip) =>
    color c = daily ? bt_engd_col : bt_engh_col
    array<box>   bs = daily ? eng_bd : eng_bh
    array<label> ls = daily ? eng_ld : eng_lh
    array.push(bs, box.new(t1, top, t2, bot, xloc=xloc.bar_time, border_color=c, border_width=1, bgcolor=color.new(c, 85)))
    array.push(ls, label.new(t2, bot, daily ? "D" : "H4", xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_up, color=c,
         textcolor=color.black, size=size.small, tooltip=tip))
    int keep = daily ? eng_n_d : eng_n_h
    while array.size(bs) > keep
        box.delete(array.shift(bs))
    while array.size(ls) > keep
        label.delete(array.shift(ls))

// The box marks the covered candle per the "covers" setting: Wick = high to low;
// Body only = its body out to its last point in the move (buys: body top down to
// the low; sells: body bottom up to the high); Both = Wick box when this engulfing
// covered the wick, else the Body box
f_eng_wickbox(string mode, bool covered_wick) =>
    mode == "Wick" ? true : mode == "Body only" ? false : covered_wick

// Weekly context sent with every bias alert (empty when there is no Weekly setup)
f_wk() =>
    bo_wk_rel == "" ? "" : ',"wk_rel":"' + bo_wk_rel + '","wk_dir":"' + bo_wk_dir + '","wk_level":' + f_num(bo_wk_lvl)
         + (bo_wk_rel == "confirmed" ? ',"wk_src":"' + bo_wk_src + '","wk_src_level":' + f_num(bo_wk_src_lvl) + ',"wk_cls":"' + bo_wk_cls + '"' : "")
f_hdrw(string t) =>
    '{"secret":"' + wh_secret + '","type":"' + t + '","timeframe":"' + timeframe.period + '","exchange":"' + syminfo.prefix + '"' + f_wk() + ',"instrument":"' + syminfo.ticker


if not na(s_bcnt) and s_bcnt > 0 and s_bcnt != last_bcnt
    last_bcnt := s_bcnt
    bool bt_same = bo_dir == s_bdir and h4_bo_fired   // same direction, H4 already riding
    bo_dir    := s_bdir
    bo_level  := s_blvl
    bo_layer  := "external"
    bo_opp    := s_bopp
    est_above := s_bdir == "bullish" and not na(d_close) and d_close > s_blvl + tol   // backtest: breakout candle's close counts
    est_below := s_bdir == "bearish" and not na(d_close) and d_close < s_blvl - tol
    retest_on := false
    retest_src:= na
    retest_kind := na
    anchor_lvl := na
    anchor_bar := na
    if not bt_same
        h4_a_lvl  := na
        h4_v_lvl  := na
    pb_consec := 0
    pb_close1 := na
    pb_oc_lvl := na
    array.clear(pb_ocs)
    retest_lvl := na
    retest_lvl2 := na
    just_broke:= true
    if not bt_same
        h4_bo_fired           := false
        h4_breaker_orig_fired := false
        h4_breaker_lvl        := na
        h4_invalid_lvl        := na
        h4_aligned            := false
        array.clear(h4_ocs)
        array.clear(h4_ocb)
        h4_brk_lvl            := na
        array.set(bt_scls, 0, "")
        e4_cls := ""
    bo_wk_rel := ""
    if not na(wk_dir)
        bo_wk_dir := wk_dir
        bo_wk_lvl := wk_level
        if s_bdir == wk_dir
            string w_cls = (not na(s_bt) and not na(wk_anchor_t) and s_bt < wk_anchor_t) ? "external" : "internal"
            if wk_react and (w_cls == "external" or bt_int)
                bo_wk_rel     := "confirmed"
                bo_wk_src     := f_wsrc_name(wk_src, wk_kind)
                bo_wk_src_lvl := wk_src_lvl
                bo_wk_cls     := w_cls
                if wk_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or wk_src == "inside_fvg"
                    bool  vb  = wk_dir == "bullish"
                    array<float> vhs = vb ? w_bf_hi : w_sf_hi
                    array<float> vls = vb ? w_bf_lo : w_sf_lo
                    int vk = array.size(vhs) - 1
                    while vk >= 0
                        if math.abs(array.get(vhs, vk) - math.max(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)) <= pip * 0.1 and math.abs(array.get(vls, vk) - math.min(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)) <= pip * 0.1
                            f_wfdrop(vhs, vls, vb ? w_bf_x : w_sf_x, vb ? w_bf_p : w_sf_p, vk)
                        vk -= 1
                else if not na(wk_src_lvl)
                    array.push(w_used, wk_src_lvl)
                if array.size(w_used) > 300
                    array.shift(w_used)
                if (wk_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or wk_src == "inside_fvg") and not na(wk_src_lvl2)
                    bool  ubull = wk_dir == "bullish"
                    float uh = math.max(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
                    float ul = math.min(wk_src_lvl, wk_src_lvl2)
                    array<float> uhs = ubull ? w_bf_hi : w_sf_hi
                    array<float> uls = ubull ? w_bf_lo : w_sf_lo
                    array<int>   uxs = ubull ? w_bf_x  : w_sf_x
                    array<bool>  ups = ubull ? w_bf_p  : w_sf_p
                    int uk = array.size(uhs) - 1
                    while uk >= 0
                        float UH = array.get(uhs, uk)
                        float UL = array.get(uls, uk)
                        if (ubull ? UL > uh : UH < ul) and f_wseen(ubull ? UH : UL)
                            f_wfdrop(uhs, uls, uxs, ups, uk)
                        uk -= 1
                wk_react    := false
                wk_src      := na
                wk_kind     := na
                wk_src_lvl  := na
                wk_src_lvl2 := na
                wk_anchor_t := na
            else
                bo_wk_rel := "inline"
        else
            bo_wk_rel := "against"
    if barstate.isrealtime
        alert(f_hdrw("BREAKOUT")
              + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","level_type":"' + bo_layer
              + '","level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
              + ',"range_level":' + f_num(bo_opp) + '}',
              alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── Daily V-/A-shapes and OCs (for inside-range reactions) ───────────────────
f_keep(array<float> a, float v) =>
    array.push(a, v)
    if array.size(a) > 120
        array.shift(a)

// A Daily level is dead once a Daily candle closes through it: buy levels (V,
// bullish OC) on a close below, sell levels (A, bearish OC) on a close above.
f_kill(array<float> a, float c, bool buy_lvl) =>
    int k = array.size(a) - 1
    while k >= 0
        float L = array.get(a, k)
        if buy_lvl ? c < L : c > L
            array.remove(a, k)
        k -= 1

if new_daily and not na(d_close)
    f_kill(d_vs,  d_close, true)
    f_kill(d_boc, d_close, true)
    f_kill(d_as,  d_close, false)
    f_kill(d_soc, d_close, false)
    if not na(bo_dir)
        f_kill(pb_ocs, d_close, bo_dir == "bullish")
        pb_oc_lvl := array.size(pb_ocs) > 0 ? array.last(pb_ocs) : na   // the label shows the newest OC still alive

if new_daily and not na(d_close2)
    bool y_bull = d_close  > d_open
    bool y_bear = d_close  < d_open
    bool p_bull = d_close2 > d_open2
    bool p_bear = d_close2 < d_open2
    if p_bear and y_bull
        f_keep(d_vs, math.min(d_low2, d_low))
    if p_bull and y_bear
        f_keep(d_as, math.max(d_high2, d_high))
    if p_bull and y_bull
        f_keep(d_boc, d_close2)
    if p_bear and y_bear
        f_keep(d_soc, d_close2)

// ── Daily engulfing in the current Daily direction ────────────────────────────
// On each completed Daily candle while a Daily direction is set: buys = the Daily
// candle before it was bearish, this one opened at or below that close and closed
// above that open (covers the body); eng_wick = it also closed above that HIGH.
// Mirror for sells. One alert (cont_type "d_engulfing"); each person picks Wick /
// Body / Both in Alert Filters, the chart labels follow "Daily engulfing covers".
if new_daily and not na(bo_dir) and not na(d_close2) and not na(dw_h2)
    bool deb = bo_dir == "bullish"
    bool d_eng = deb ? (d_close2 < d_open2 and d_close > d_open and d_open <= d_close2 and d_close > d_open2)
                     : (d_close2 > d_open2 and d_close < d_open and d_open >= d_close2 and d_close < d_open2)
    if d_eng
        bool  d_eng_wick = deb ? d_close > dw_h2 : d_close < dw_l2
        float d_eng_lvl  = d_eng_wick ? (deb ? dw_h2 : dw_l2) : d_open2
        if bt_deng_mode != "Wick" or d_eng_wick
            f_btlbl(deb, 11, "", d_eng_lvl, bo_level, d_eng_wick ? "Covers the previous Daily candle's wick" : "Covers the previous Daily candle's body only")
            // the box shows on the Daily chart and every lower timeframe
            if bt_show and bt_dengulf and time >= bt_from and not na(dw_t2) and timeframe.in_seconds() <= 86400
                bool  ewb    = f_eng_wickbox(bt_deng_mode, d_eng_wick)
                float eb_top = ewb or not deb ? dw_h2 : math.max(d_open2, d_close2)   // the covered Daily candle
                float eb_bot = ewb or deb ? dw_l2 : math.min(d_open2, d_close2)
                f_eng_draw(true, dw_t2, time[1], eb_top, eb_bot, syminfo.ticker + "\nDaily " + (deb ? "buy" : "sell") + " engulfing candle has formed\n" + (d_eng_wick ? "Covers the previous Daily candle's wick" : "Covers the previous Daily candle's body only"))
        if barstate.isrealtime
            alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                  + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"d_engulfing","eng_wick":' + (d_eng_wick ? "true" : "false")
                  + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                  + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(d_eng_lvl) + '}',
                  alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── Daily OC formed (notification) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// On each completed Daily candle while a Daily direction is set: it and the Daily
// candle before it are both bullish (buys; bearish for sells). Level = where the
// first one closed. Only the pair and "Daily OC has formed" (cont_type "d_oc_formed").
if new_daily and not na(bo_dir) and not na(d_close2)
    bool docb = bo_dir == "bullish"
    if docb ? (d_close2 > d_open2 and d_close > d_open) : (d_close2 < d_open2 and d_close < d_open)
        if bt_docf and time >= bt_from and timeframe.in_seconds() <= 86400
            label.delete(ocf_d)
            ocf_d := label.new(time[1], docb ? dr_l : dr_h, "✕", xloc=xloc.bar_time,
                 style=docb ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.black, 100),
                 textcolor=bt_ocf_col, size=size.small,
                 tooltip=syminfo.ticker + "\nDaily OC has formed\nOC level " + str.tostring(d_close2, format.mintick))
        if barstate.isrealtime
            alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                  + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"d_oc_formed"'
                  + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                  + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(d_close2) + '}',
                  alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// Daily FVGs. A gap is only an FVG once its third Daily candle has closed. A Daily
// close through the gap kills it (bullish: below the bottom; bearish: above the top).
f_fvg_drop(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<float> xs, array<int> xbs, array<bool> ps, int k) =>
    array.remove(his, k)
    array.remove(los, k)
    array.remove(xs, k)
    array.remove(xbs, k)
    array.remove(ps, k)
f_fvg_kill(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<float> xs, array<int> xbs, array<bool> ps, float c, bool bull) =>
    int k = array.size(his) - 1
    while k >= 0
        if bull ? c < array.get(los, k) : c > array.get(his, k)
            f_fvg_drop(his, los, xs, xbs, ps, k)
        k -= 1
f_fvg_keep(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<float> xs, array<int> xbs, array<bool> ps, float h, float l) =>
    array.push(his, h)
    array.push(los, l)
    array.push(xs, na)
    array.push(xbs, na)
    array.push(ps, false)
    if array.size(his) > 60
        f_fvg_drop(his, los, xs, xbs, ps, 0)
// Index of the FVG with this top / bottom, or -1
f_fvg_idx(array<float> his, array<float> los, float h, float l) =>
    int found = -1
    if array.size(his) > 0 and not na(h) and not na(l)
        for i = 0 to array.size(his) - 1
            if math.abs(array.get(his, i) - h) <= pip * 0.1 and math.abs(array.get(los, i) - l) <= pip * 0.1
                found := i
    found

if new_daily and not na(d_close)
    f_fvg_kill(d_bf_hi, d_bf_lo, d_bf_x, d_bf_xb, d_bf_p, d_close, true)
    f_fvg_kill(d_sf_hi, d_sf_lo, d_sf_x, d_sf_xb, d_sf_p, d_close, false)
if new_daily and not na(dg_h3) and not na(dg_l1)
    // The middle candle can be anything (even the Daily breakout candle): the gap
    // only exists once the third candle closes without reaching the first one.
    if dg_l1 > dg_h3
        f_fvg_keep(d_bf_hi, d_bf_lo, d_bf_x, d_bf_xb, d_bf_p, dg_l1, dg_h3)
    if dg_h1 < dg_l3
        f_fvg_keep(d_sf_hi, d_sf_lo, d_sf_x, d_sf_xb, d_sf_p, dg_l3, dg_h1)

f_used(float L) =>
    bool found = false
    for x in d_used
        if math.abs(x - L) <= pip * 0.1
            found := true
    found

// Deepest Daily FVG this H4 candle's wick enters. inside: the whole gap sits inside
// the range that was just broken; otherwise the gap reaches beyond the Daily Breaker
// (after the breakout, incl. the breakout candle's own gap). Returns its index, or -1.
f_fvg_pick(array<float> his, array<float> los, array<bool> ps, bool bull, bool inside, float opp, float b_lo, float b_hi) =>
    int   best = -1
    float bv   = na
    if array.size(his) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(his) - 1
            float H = array.get(his, i)
            float L = array.get(los, i)
            bool in_pos  = inside ? (not na(opp) and (bull ? (L > opp and H < b_lo) : (H < opp and L > b_hi))) : (bull ? H > b_hi : L < b_lo)
            bool touched = low <= H and high >= L
            float edge   = bull ? L : H
            if in_pos and touched and not array.get(ps, i) and (na(bv) or (bull ? edge < bv : edge > bv))
                bv   := edge
                best := i
    best

// Deepest Daily level in `lv` that sits inside the broken range and that this
// H4 candle touches exactly and holds (buy: lowest; sell: highest).
f_ir_pick(array<float> lv, bool bull, float opp, float b_lo, float b_hi, float t) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(lv) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lv) - 1
            float L = array.get(lv, i)
            bool inside  = bull ? (L > opp and L < b_lo) : (L < opp and L > b_hi)
            bool touched = low <= L and high >= L
            bool held    = bull ? close >= L - t : close <= L + t
            if inside and touched and held and not f_used(L) and (na(best) or (bull ? L < best : L > best))
                best := L
    best

// Daily V-shapes (A-shapes for sells) beyond the Daily Breaker: formed in the move
// after the breakout. Deepest one this H4 candle touches exactly and holds.
f_pv_pick(array<float> lv, bool bull, float b_lo, float b_hi, float t) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(lv) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lv) - 1
            float L = array.get(lv, i)
            bool beyond  = bull ? L > b_hi : L < b_lo
            bool touched = low <= L and high >= L
            bool held    = bull ? close >= L - t : close <= L + t
            if beyond and touched and held and not f_used(L) and (na(best) or (bull ? L < best : L > best))
                best := L
    best

f_bt_seen(float L) =>
    bool found = false
    for x in bt_seen
        if math.abs(x - L) <= pip * 0.1
            found := true
    found

// ── Post-breakout OC tracking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
if new_daily and not na(bo_dir) and not just_broke
    bool d_bull = d_close >= d_open
    bool d_bear = d_close <  d_open
    bool pb_match = false
    if bo_dir == "bullish"
        pb_match := d_bull and d_close > bo_level
    else
        pb_match := d_bear and d_close < bo_level
    if pb_match
        pb_consec := pb_consec + 1
        if pb_consec == 1
            pb_close1 := d_close
        else if pb_consec >= 2
            pb_oc_lvl  := pb_close1
            array.push(pb_ocs, pb_close1)
            if array.size(pb_ocs) > 30
                array.shift(pb_ocs)
            poc_origin := bar_index
            pb_close1  := d_close
    else
        pb_consec := 0

// Keep only the H4 OCs formed from the breakout leg's swing low (buy) / high
// (sell) onward: the extreme between the broken A/V's formation and now.
f_h4_leg_prune(array<float> lv, array<int> lb, int from_bar, bool bull) =>
    int   ext_bar = bar_index
    float ext     = bull ? low : high
    int   n       = math.min(bar_index - nz(from_bar, bar_index), 400)
    for i = 0 to n
        if bull ? low[i] < ext : high[i] > ext
            ext     := bull ? low[i] : high[i]
            ext_bar := bar_index - i
    int k = array.size(lb) - 1
    while k >= 0
        if array.get(lb, k) < ext_bar
            array.remove(lv, k)
            array.remove(lb, k)
        k -= 1

// A new H4 breakout in line: its retest levels are the Breaker and the H4 V-shapes
// (A-shapes for sells) formed from the leg's swing low (high) onward that sit below
// (above) the Breaker. Nothing retested yet.
f_rt_arm(bool bull, int from_bar, float brk) =>
    int   ext_bar = bar_index
    float ext     = bull ? low : high
    int   n       = math.min(bar_index - nz(from_bar, bar_index), 400)
    for i = 0 to n
        if bull ? low[i] < ext : high[i] > ext
            ext     := bull ? low[i] : high[i]
            ext_bar := bar_index - i
    array.clear(rt_lvls)
    array.set(rt_held, 0, false)
    if not na(brk)
        array.push(rt_lvls, brk)
    array<float> lv = bull ? vh_lv : ah_lv
    array<int>   lb = bull ? vh_b  : ah_b
    int sz = array.size(lv)
    if sz > 0
        for k = 0 to sz - 1
            float rv = array.get(lv, k)
            if array.get(lb, k) >= ext_bar and (na(brk) or (bull ? rv < brk : rv > brk))
                array.push(rt_lvls, rv)

// ── H4 liquidity sweeps (display only, like LuxAlgo "Liquidity Sweeps", wicks) ─
// A swing low = a low lower than the sw_len candles on each side (known sw_len
// candles later). A candle whose wick goes below a live swing low and closes back
// above it SWEEPS it (once); a close below the swing low ends it. Mirror for highs.
// Every sweep on the chart: dotted line swing → sweep candle, zone over the wick
f_sw_mark(bool bull, float lv, int pb) =>
    if sw_all and timeframe.period == "240"
        color zc = bull ? sw_bull_col : sw_bear_col
        if sw_lmode != "Hide"
            array.push(sw_all_l, line.new(pb, lv, bar_index, lv, color=color.new(zc, 0), style=line.style_dotted, extend=sw_lmode == "Extend right" ? extend.right : extend.none))
        array.push(sw_all_b, box.new(bar_index - 1, bull ? lv : high, bar_index + 1, bull ? low : lv, border_color=color.new(zc, 100), bgcolor=zc))
        array.push(sw_all_d, bull)
        array.push(sw_all_x, false)
        if array.size(sw_all_l) > 200
            line.delete(array.shift(sw_all_l))
        if array.size(sw_all_b) > 200
            box.delete(array.shift(sw_all_b))
            array.shift(sw_all_d)
            array.shift(sw_all_x)

float sw_pl = ta.pivotlow(low, sw_len, sw_len)
float sw_ph = ta.pivothigh(high, sw_len, sw_len)
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(sw_pl)
        array.push(sw_pl_p, sw_pl)
        array.push(sw_pl_b, bar_index - sw_len)
    if not na(sw_ph)
        array.push(sw_ph_p, sw_ph)
        array.push(sw_ph_b, bar_index - sw_len)
    int sk = array.size(sw_pl_p) - 1
    while sk >= 0
        float sp = array.get(sw_pl_p, sk)
        bool  old = bar_index - array.get(sw_pl_b, sk) > 2000
        if close < sp or old
            array.remove(sw_pl_p, sk)
            array.remove(sw_pl_b, sk)
        else if low < sp and close > sp and array.get(sw_pl_b, sk) < bar_index
            array.push(swb_bar, bar_index)
            array.push(swb_lvl, sp)
            array.push(swb_piv, array.get(sw_pl_b, sk))
            f_sw_mark(true, sp, array.get(sw_pl_b, sk))
            array.remove(sw_pl_p, sk)
            array.remove(sw_pl_b, sk)
        sk -= 1
    sk := array.size(sw_ph_p) - 1
    while sk >= 0
        float sp = array.get(sw_ph_p, sk)
        bool  old = bar_index - array.get(sw_ph_b, sk) > 2000
        if close > sp or old
            array.remove(sw_ph_p, sk)
            array.remove(sw_ph_b, sk)
        else if high > sp and close < sp and array.get(sw_ph_b, sk) < bar_index
            array.push(sws_bar, bar_index)
            array.push(sws_lvl, sp)
            array.push(sws_piv, array.get(sw_ph_b, sk))
            f_sw_mark(false, sp, array.get(sw_ph_b, sk))
            array.remove(sw_ph_p, sk)
            array.remove(sw_ph_b, sk)
        sk -= 1
    // Extend each live zone to this candle until a close goes through it (like LuxAlgo)
    if sw_ext and array.size(sw_all_b) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(sw_all_b) - 1
            if not array.get(sw_all_x, i)
                box zb = array.get(sw_all_b, i)
                if bar_index - box.get_left(zb) - 1 <= sw_maxb
                    box.set_right(zb, bar_index)
                    if array.get(sw_all_d, i) ? close < box.get_bottom(zb) : close > box.get_top(zb)
                        array.set(sw_all_x, i, true)
                else
                    array.set(sw_all_x, i, true)
    while array.size(swb_bar) > 200
        array.shift(swb_bar)
        array.shift(swb_lvl)
        array.shift(swb_piv)
    while array.size(sws_bar) > 200
        array.shift(sws_bar)
        array.shift(sws_lvl)
        array.shift(sws_piv)

// The bar the broken H4 level formed on: buys an A-shape (bull then bear candle,
// level = the bull candle's body top), sells a V-shape. na if not found.
f_lvl_bar(bool bull, float lvl) =>
    int found = na
    int lim = math.min(bar_index - 2, 400)
    for i = 1 to lim
        bool shape = bull ? (close[i] < open[i] and close[i + 1] >= open[i + 1]) : (close[i] >= open[i] and close[i + 1] < open[i + 1])
        float v = bull ? math.max(open[i + 1], close[i + 1]) : math.min(open[i + 1], close[i + 1])
        if shape and math.abs(v - lvl) <= syminfo.mintick
            found := bar_index - i
            break
    found

// The label line for an H4 breakout after a Daily reaction: did an H4 candle sweep
// a swing low (high, sells) during this break, i.e. from when the broken level
// formed up to this breakout candle? Draws a line at the swept level.
f_sw_note(bool bull, float brk) =>
    string out = ""
    if bt_sweep and timeframe.period == "240"
        int fromb = f_lvl_bar(bull, brk)
        fromb := na(fromb) ? bar_index - 60 : fromb
        array<int>   bars = bull ? swb_bar : sws_bar
        array<float> lvls = bull ? swb_lvl : sws_lvl
        array<int>   pivs = bull ? swb_piv : sws_piv
        int hit = -1
        if array.size(bars) > 0
            for k = array.size(bars) - 1 to 0
                int b = array.get(bars, k)
                if b < fromb
                    break
                if b <= bar_index
                    hit := k
                    break
        if hit >= 0
            float lv = array.get(lvls, hit)
            out := "✓ swept H4 " + (bull ? "low " : "high ") + str.tostring(lv, format.mintick) + " before the break"
            array.push(sw_lines, line.new(array.get(pivs, hit), lv, array.get(bars, hit), lv, color=sw_col, style=line.style_dotted, width=2))
            if array.size(sw_lines) > 25
                line.delete(array.shift(sw_lines))
        else
            out := "✗ no sweep before the break"
    out

// D.A / D.V (wick levels): only the one in line with the last breakout is
// monitored — D.V in a bullish bias, D.A in a bearish bias.
float a_lvl = bo_dir == "bullish" ? na : s_da
float v_lvl = bo_dir == "bearish" ? na : s_dv

// ── H4 block ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(bo_dir) and not na(bo_level) and timeframe.period == "240"
    float band_hi = bo_level + tol
    float band_lo = bo_level - tol
    bool  bk_sent = false   // an H4 Breaker alert went out on this candle

    // The H4 A / V that stood BEFORE this candle. A reaction's External level is
    // the last level formed before the candle that touched the Daily level; an
    // A / V completed by that candle itself (or later) is Internal.
    float pre_a = h4_a_lvl
    float pre_v = h4_v_lvl

    // ── H4 formation detection ────────────────────────────────────────────
    bool h4_bull1 = close[1] >= open[1]
    bool h4_bear1 = close[1] <  open[1]
    bool h4_bull0 = close    >= open
    bool h4_bear0 = close    <  open

    bool new_a = h4_bull1 and h4_bear0
    if new_a
        h4_a_lvl   := math.max(open[1], close[1])
        h4a_origin := bar_index
        array.push(ah_lv, h4_a_lvl)
        array.push(ah_b, bar_index)
        if array.size(ah_lv) > 60
            array.shift(ah_lv)
            array.shift(ah_b)

    bool new_v = h4_bear1 and h4_bull0
    if new_v
        h4_v_lvl   := math.min(open[1], close[1])
        h4v_origin := bar_index
        array.push(vh_lv, h4_v_lvl)
        array.push(vh_b, bar_index)
        if array.size(vh_lv) > 60
            array.shift(vh_lv)
            array.shift(vh_b)

    // ── H4 FVG after an H4 breakout in line with the Daily ────────────────
    // Checked once, on the candle right after the breakout candle. Buys: its low
    // stays above the high of the candle before the breakout (sells: mirror).
    if not na(h4f_bar) and bar_index == h4f_bar + 1
        bool fvg_ok = h4_bo_fired and (h4f_bull == (bo_dir == "bullish")) and (h4f_bull ? low > h4f_ref : high < h4f_ref)
        if fvg_ok
            float fv_lo = h4f_bull ? h4f_ref : high
            float fv_hi = h4f_bull ? low : h4f_ref
            f_btlbl(h4f_bull, 10, "", h4f_ref, bo_level, "H4 FVG " + str.tostring(fv_lo, format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(fv_hi, format.mintick))
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"h4_fvg"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(h4f_ref)
                      + ',"fvg_low":' + str.tostring(fv_lo) + ',"fvg_high":' + str.tostring(fv_hi) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if not na(h4f_bar) and bar_index > h4f_bar
        h4f_bar := na

    // ── Establishment tracking ────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Read BEFORE this bar updates it: "an EARLIER H4 bar closed beyond the band".
    // (est_above[1] leaked the previous breakout's flag onto the bar of a new
    // same-direction breakout, letting it count as a retest without moving away.)
    bool was_est = (bo_dir == "bullish") ? est_above : est_below
    if bo_dir == "bullish" and close > band_hi
        est_above := true
    if bo_dir == "bearish" and close < band_lo
        est_below := true

    // ── Zone 1: Post-Breakout OCs ─────────────────────────────────────────
    // Every completed post-breakout OC stays eligible until an opposing daily
    // breakout. Use the deepest one this H4 bar reacts from (lowest for a buy,
    // highest for a sell) whose close hasn't gone through it.
    float pb_hit = na
    if array.size(pb_ocs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pb_ocs) - 1
            float oc = array.get(pb_ocs, i)
            bool beyond  = (bo_dir == "bullish" and oc > band_hi) or (bo_dir == "bearish" and oc < band_lo)
            bool touched = low <= oc and high >= oc
            bool held    = bo_dir == "bullish" ? close >= oc - tol : close <= oc + tol
            if beyond and touched and held and not f_used(oc)
                if na(pb_hit) or (bo_dir == "bullish" ? oc < pb_hit : oc > pb_hit)
                    pb_hit := oc
    bool pb_oc_zone = not na(pb_hit)

    // ── Zone 2: Daily Breaker ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    bool db_zone = low <= bo_level and high >= bo_level and (bo_dir == "bullish" ? close >= band_lo : close <= band_hi) and not f_used(bo_level)

    // ── Zone 3: Inside Range ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Inside the range that was just broken, only a reaction from a Daily
    // V-shape (A-shape for sells) or Daily OC level counts: the H4 wick reaches
    // the exact level and the close doesn't go through it. Deepest level wins.
    float  ir_hit  = na
    string ir_kind = na
    if not na(bo_opp)
        bool  bull = bo_dir == "bullish"
        float shp  = na
        float occ  = na
        if bull
            shp := f_ir_pick(d_vs,  true,  bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi, tol)
            occ := f_ir_pick(d_boc, true,  bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi, tol)
        else
            shp := f_ir_pick(d_as,  false, bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi, tol)
            occ := f_ir_pick(d_soc, false, bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi, tol)
        if not na(shp)
            ir_hit  := shp
            ir_kind := bull ? "v_shape" : "a_shape"
        if not na(occ) and (na(ir_hit) or (bull ? occ < ir_hit : occ > ir_hit))
            ir_hit  := occ
            ir_kind := "oc"
    bool ir_zone = not na(ir_hit)

    // ── Zone 4 (backtest): Daily V/A-shape after the breakout ─────────────
    float pv_hit  = f_pv_pick(bo_dir == "bullish" ? d_vs : d_as, bo_dir == "bullish", band_lo, band_hi, tol)
    bool  pv_zone = not na(pv_hit)

    // ── Zone 5 (backtest): Daily FVGs, after the breakout and inside the range ─
    bool  fz_bull = bo_dir == "bullish"
    array<float> fz_his = fz_bull ? d_bf_hi : d_sf_hi
    array<float> fz_los = fz_bull ? d_bf_lo : d_sf_lo
    array<float> fz_x   = fz_bull ? d_bf_x  : d_sf_x
    array<int>   fz_xb  = fz_bull ? d_bf_xb : d_sf_xb
    array<bool>  fz_p   = fz_bull ? d_bf_p  : d_sf_p
    int   pf_i = bt_dfvg ? f_fvg_pick(fz_his, fz_los, fz_p, fz_bull, false, bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi) : -1
    int   if_i = bt_dfvg ? f_fvg_pick(fz_his, fz_los, fz_p, fz_bull, true,  bo_opp, band_lo, band_hi) : -1

    // ── Backtest: first H4 touch of each Daily level since it formed ──────
    bool bt_bull = bo_dir == "bullish"
    array<float> bt_cand = array.new<float>()
    array.push(bt_cand, bo_level)
    for L in pb_ocs
        array.push(bt_cand, L)
    array<float> bt_shp = bt_bull ? d_vs : d_as
    array<float> bt_ocl = bt_bull ? d_boc : d_soc
    for L in bt_shp
        array.push(bt_cand, L)
    for L in bt_ocl
        array.push(bt_cand, L)
    bool bt_first = false
    for L in bt_cand
        bool bt_held = bt_bull ? close >= L - tol : close <= L + tol
        if low <= L and high >= L and bt_held and not f_bt_seen(L)
            array.push(bt_seen, L)
            bt_first := true
    if bt_dfvg and array.size(fz_his) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fz_his) - 1
            float fH = array.get(fz_his, i)
            float fL = array.get(fz_los, i)
            float fK = bt_bull ? fH : fL
            if low <= fH and high >= fL and not f_bt_seen(fK)
                array.push(bt_seen, fK)
                bt_first := true
                array.set(fz_x, i, bt_bull ? pre_a : pre_v)
                array.set(fz_xb, i, bar_index)
    if array.size(bt_seen) > 300
        array.shift(bt_seen)
    if bt_first
        anchor_bar := bar_index
        bt_ext_a   := pre_a
        bt_ext_v   := pre_v

    // ── RETEST_CANCELLED — only when the reaction FAILS ───────────────────
    // A reaction stays valid on later candles: any later H4 close beyond the
    // H4 A/V level still confirms it. It fails only when an H4 candle closes
    // back through the zone on the wrong side; then the next zone price
    // reaches (checked just below, on this same bar) takes over.
    if retest_on
        bool failed = false
        if retest_src == "post_breakout_oc"
            failed := bo_dir == "bullish" ? close < retest_lvl - tol : close > retest_lvl + tol
        else if retest_src == "daily_breaker"
            failed := bo_dir == "bullish" ? close < band_lo : close > band_hi
        else if retest_src == "inside_range"
            failed := bo_dir == "bullish" ? close < retest_lvl - tol : close > retest_lvl + tol
        else if retest_src == "post_breakout_v"
            failed := bo_dir == "bullish" ? close < retest_lvl - tol : close > retest_lvl + tol
        else if retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg"
            failed := new_daily and not na(d_close) and (bo_dir == "bullish" ? d_close < retest_lvl2 : d_close > retest_lvl2)

        if failed
            // A failed reaction uses the level too: only its first touch counts
            if not (retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg") and not na(retest_lvl)
                array.push(d_used, retest_lvl)
            retest_on  := false
            retest_src := na
            retest_lvl := na
            retest_lvl2 := na
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST_CANCELLED") + '"}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)

    // ── RETEST detection ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Before the Origin, and again whenever H4 is out of line: H4 only counts
    // a break back in the daily direction after a fresh daily reaction.
    if not retest_on
        if pb_oc_zone and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "post_breakout_oc"
            retest_lvl2 := na
            retest_lvl := pb_hit
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // backtest: normally set by the first-touch scan below
                anchor_lvl := pb_hit
                anchor_bar := bar_index
                bt_ext_a   := pre_a
                bt_ext_v   := pre_v
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","source":"post_breakout_oc"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(pb_hit) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        else if pv_zone and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "post_breakout_v"
            retest_lvl2 := na
            retest_lvl := pv_hit
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // backtest: normally set by the first-touch scan below
                anchor_lvl := pv_hit
                anchor_bar := bar_index
                bt_ext_a   := pre_a
                bt_ext_v   := pre_v
        else if pf_i >= 0 and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "post_breakout_fvg"
            retest_lvl := fz_bull ? array.get(fz_his, pf_i) : array.get(fz_los, pf_i)
            retest_lvl2 := fz_bull ? array.get(fz_los, pf_i) : array.get(fz_his, pf_i)
            fz_day_bar  := na   // today's entry into this FVG is looked for afresh
            fz_day_done := false
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // this FVG's own External level (set when a candle first entered it)
                float fx = array.get(fz_x, pf_i)
                anchor_lvl := retest_lvl
                anchor_bar := na(fx) ? bar_index : array.get(fz_xb, pf_i)
                bt_ext_a   := na(fx) or not fz_bull ? pre_a : fx
                bt_ext_v   := na(fx) or fz_bull ? pre_v : fx
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","source":"post_breakout_fvg"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl) + ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        else if db_zone and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "daily_breaker"
            retest_lvl2 := na
            retest_lvl := bo_level
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // backtest: normally set by the first-touch scan below
                anchor_lvl := bo_level
                anchor_bar := bar_index
                bt_ext_a   := pre_a
                bt_ext_v   := pre_v
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","source":"daily_breaker"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        else if ir_zone and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "inside_range"
            retest_lvl2 := na
            retest_lvl := ir_hit
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // backtest: normally set by the first-touch scan below
                anchor_lvl := ir_hit
                anchor_bar := bar_index
                bt_ext_a   := pre_a
                bt_ext_v   := pre_v
            retest_kind := ir_kind
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","source":"inside_range","source_kind":"' + ir_kind + '"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(ir_hit) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        else if if_i >= 0 and was_est
            retest_on  := true
            retest_bar := bar_index
            retest_src := "inside_fvg"
            retest_lvl := fz_bull ? array.get(fz_his, if_i) : array.get(fz_los, if_i)
            retest_lvl2 := fz_bull ? array.get(fz_los, if_i) : array.get(fz_his, if_i)
            fz_day_bar  := na   // today's entry into this FVG is looked for afresh
            fz_day_done := false
            if na(anchor_lvl)   // this FVG's own External level (set when a candle first entered it)
                float fx = array.get(fz_x, if_i)
                anchor_lvl := retest_lvl
                anchor_bar := na(fx) ? bar_index : array.get(fz_xb, if_i)
                bt_ext_a   := na(fx) or not fz_bull ? pre_a : fx
                bt_ext_v   := na(fx) or fz_bull ? pre_v : fx
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdr("RETEST")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","source":"inside_fvg"'
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl) + ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)

    // ── Daily FVG reactions: each deeper Daily candle restarts the check ──
    // A Daily FVG is a zone, so the reaction moves with price. While price reacts
    // inside it, a Daily candle that dips below the previous Daily candle's low
    // (above its high for sells) becomes the reaction: the External H4 level is
    // the latest H4 A (V for sells) from when that Daily candle first entered the
    // FVG. A higher H4 A made after the earlier reaction is no longer External.
    if new_daily
        fz_day_bar  := na
        fz_day_done := false
    bool fz_on = retest_on and (retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg")
    // While reacting at an FVG, price entering a DEEPER FVG (wholly below it for
    // buys, above for sells) moves the reaction there, with that FVG's own
    // External level (from the candle that first entered it).
    if fz_on
        float cur_hi = math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
        float cur_lo = math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
        int   dk = -1
        if array.size(fz_his) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(fz_his) - 1
                float gH = array.get(fz_his, i)
                float gL = array.get(fz_los, i)
                bool deeper = fz_bull ? gH < cur_lo : gL > cur_hi
                bool ok_pos = fz_bull ? (gH > band_hi or (not na(bo_opp) and gL > bo_opp and gH < band_lo)) : (gL < band_lo or (not na(bo_opp) and gH < bo_opp and gL > band_hi))
                if deeper and ok_pos and not array.get(fz_p, i) and low <= gH and high >= gL and (dk < 0 or (fz_bull ? gL < array.get(fz_los, dk) : gH > array.get(fz_his, dk)))
                    dk := i
        if dk >= 0
            float dH = array.get(fz_his, dk)
            float dL = array.get(fz_los, dk)
            retest_src  := (fz_bull ? dH > band_hi : dL < band_lo) ? "post_breakout_fvg" : "inside_fvg"
            retest_lvl  := fz_bull ? dH : dL
            retest_lvl2 := fz_bull ? dL : dH
            retest_bar  := bar_index
            float fx2 = array.get(fz_x, dk)
            anchor_lvl  := retest_lvl
            anchor_bar  := na(fx2) ? bar_index : array.get(fz_xb, dk)
            if fz_bull
                bt_ext_a := na(fx2) ? pre_a : fx2
            else
                bt_ext_v := na(fx2) ? pre_v : fx2
            fz_day_bar  := na
            fz_day_done := false
    if fz_on and na(fz_day_bar) and low <= math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2) and high >= math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
        fz_day_bar := bar_index
        fz_day_a   := pre_a
        fz_day_v   := pre_v
    if fz_on and not fz_day_done and not na(fz_day_bar) and not na(dr_l) and (bo_dir == "bullish" ? low < dr_l : high > dr_h)
        fz_day_done := true
        anchor_bar  := fz_day_bar
        bt_ext_a    := fz_day_a
        bt_ext_v    := fz_day_v
        int ak = f_fvg_idx(fz_his, fz_los, math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2), math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2))
        if ak >= 0
            array.set(fz_x, ak, fz_bull ? fz_day_a : fz_day_v)
            array.set(fz_xb, ak, fz_day_bar)

    // ── Pierced Daily FVGs (after this candle's reaction checks) ──────────
    if array.size(d_bf_lo) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(d_bf_lo) - 1
            if low < array.get(d_bf_lo, i)
                array.set(d_bf_p, i, true)
    if array.size(d_sf_hi) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(d_sf_hi) - 1
            if high > array.get(d_sf_hi, i)
                array.set(d_sf_p, i, true)

    // ── H4 CONFIRMED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    bool confirmed_this_bar = false

    if retest_on
        float src_lvl = na(retest_lvl) ? bo_level : retest_lvl
        bool  bt_was_aligned = h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned   // a fresh Daily reaction while H4 is still aligned

        bool bt_xb = not na(bt_ext_a) and close > bt_ext_a                      // External level broken
        bool bt_lb = not na(h4_a_lvl) and not new_a and close > h4_a_lvl       // latest A broken
        if bo_dir == "bullish" and (bt_xb or (bt_lb and (h4a_origin < anchor_bar or bt_int)))
            string h4_cls = (bt_xb or h4a_origin < anchor_bar) ? "external" : "internal"
            e4_cls := h4_cls
            float  bt_brk = bt_xb ? bt_ext_a : h4_a_lvl
            if not h4_bo_fired
                h4_bo_fired           := true
                h4_aligned            := true
                h4_breaker_lvl        := bt_brk
                bk_origin             := bar_index
                h4_invalid_lvl        := h4_v_lvl
                h4_brk_lvl            := h4_a_lvl
                f_h4_leg_prune(h4_ocs, h4_ocb, h4a_origin, true)
                f_rt_arm(true, h4a_origin, bt_brk)
                h4_breaker_orig_fired := false
                confirmed_this_bar    := true
                bt_swtxt := f_sw_note(true, bt_brk)
                f_btlbl(true, 0, h4_cls, bt_brk, bo_level, "Daily reaction: " + f_bt_src(retest_src) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(src_lvl))
                if barstate.isrealtime
                    alert(f_hdrw("CONFIRMED")
                          + '","direction":"bullish","source":"' + retest_src
                          + '","h4_class":"' + h4_cls
                          + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                          + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(src_lvl)
                          + (retest_src == "inside_range" and not na(retest_kind) ? ',"source_kind":"' + retest_kind + '"' : '')
                          + (na(retest_lvl2) ? '' : ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2))
                          + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(bt_brk) + '}',
                          alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else
                h4_aligned            := true
                h4_breaker_lvl        := bt_brk
                bk_origin             := bar_index
                h4_invalid_lvl        := h4_v_lvl
                h4_brk_lvl            := h4_a_lvl
                f_h4_leg_prune(h4_ocs, h4_ocb, h4a_origin, true)
                f_rt_arm(true, h4a_origin, bt_brk)
                confirmed_this_bar    := true
                bt_swtxt := f_sw_note(true, bt_brk)
                f_btlbl(true, bt_was_aligned ? 7 : 1, h4_cls, bt_brk, bo_level, "Daily reaction: " + f_bt_src(retest_src) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(src_lvl))
                if barstate.isrealtime
                    alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                          + '","direction":"bullish","cont_type":"' + (bt_was_aligned ? "daily_react" : "breakout_cont") + '","h4_class":"' + h4_cls + '"'
                          + ',"source":"' + retest_src + '","source_level":' + str.tostring(src_lvl)
                          + (retest_src == "inside_range" and not na(retest_kind) ? ',"source_kind":"' + retest_kind + '"' : '')
                          + (na(retest_lvl2) ? '' : ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2))
                          + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                          + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(bt_brk) + '}',
                          alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            // The level has given its alert: it is used (first touch is the one that counts)
            if retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg"
                int uk0 = f_fvg_idx(fz_his, fz_los, math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2), math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2))
                if uk0 >= 0
                    f_fvg_drop(fz_his, fz_los, fz_x, fz_xb, fz_p, uk0)
            else if not na(retest_lvl)
                array.push(d_used, retest_lvl)
                if array.size(d_used) > 300
                    array.shift(d_used)
            if (retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg") and array.size(fz_his) > 0
                float uh = math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
                float ul = math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
                int uk = array.size(fz_his) - 1
                while uk >= 0
                    float UH = array.get(fz_his, uk)
                    float UL = array.get(fz_los, uk)
                    if (fz_bull ? UL > uh : UH < ul) and f_bt_seen(fz_bull ? UH : UL)
                        f_fvg_drop(fz_his, fz_los, fz_x, fz_xb, fz_p, uk)
                    uk -= 1
            retest_on  := false
            retest_src := na
            retest_lvl := na
            retest_lvl2 := na
            anchor_lvl := na

        bool bt_xs = not na(bt_ext_v) and close < bt_ext_v
        bool bt_ls = not na(h4_v_lvl) and not new_v and close < h4_v_lvl
        if bo_dir == "bearish" and (bt_xs or (bt_ls and (h4v_origin < anchor_bar or bt_int)))
            string h4_cls = (bt_xs or h4v_origin < anchor_bar) ? "external" : "internal"
            e4_cls := h4_cls
            float  bt_brkv = bt_xs ? bt_ext_v : h4_v_lvl
            if not h4_bo_fired
                h4_bo_fired           := true
                h4_aligned            := true
                h4_breaker_lvl        := bt_brkv
                bk_origin             := bar_index
                h4_invalid_lvl        := h4_a_lvl
                h4_brk_lvl            := h4_v_lvl
                f_h4_leg_prune(h4_ocs, h4_ocb, h4v_origin, false)
                f_rt_arm(false, h4v_origin, bt_brkv)
                h4_breaker_orig_fired := false
                confirmed_this_bar    := true
                bt_swtxt := f_sw_note(false, bt_brkv)
                f_btlbl(false, 0, h4_cls, bt_brkv, bo_level, "Daily reaction: " + f_bt_src(retest_src) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(src_lvl))
                if barstate.isrealtime
                    alert(f_hdrw("CONFIRMED")
                          + '","direction":"bearish","source":"' + retest_src
                          + '","h4_class":"' + h4_cls
                          + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                          + ',"source_level":' + str.tostring(src_lvl)
                          + (retest_src == "inside_range" and not na(retest_kind) ? ',"source_kind":"' + retest_kind + '"' : '')
                          + (na(retest_lvl2) ? '' : ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2))
                          + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(bt_brkv) + '}',
                          alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else
                h4_aligned            := true
                h4_breaker_lvl        := bt_brkv
                bk_origin             := bar_index
                h4_invalid_lvl        := h4_a_lvl
                h4_brk_lvl            := h4_v_lvl
                f_h4_leg_prune(h4_ocs, h4_ocb, h4v_origin, false)
                f_rt_arm(false, h4v_origin, bt_brkv)
                confirmed_this_bar    := true
                bt_swtxt := f_sw_note(false, bt_brkv)
                f_btlbl(false, bt_was_aligned ? 7 : 1, h4_cls, bt_brkv, bo_level, "Daily reaction: " + f_bt_src(retest_src) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(src_lvl))
                if barstate.isrealtime
                    alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                          + '","direction":"bearish","cont_type":"' + (bt_was_aligned ? "daily_react" : "breakout_cont") + '","h4_class":"' + h4_cls + '"'
                          + ',"source":"' + retest_src + '","source_level":' + str.tostring(src_lvl)
                          + (retest_src == "inside_range" and not na(retest_kind) ? ',"source_kind":"' + retest_kind + '"' : '')
                          + (na(retest_lvl2) ? '' : ',"source_level2":' + str.tostring(retest_lvl2))
                          + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                          + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(bt_brkv) + '}',
                          alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            // The level has given its alert: it is used (first touch is the one that counts)
            if retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg"
                int uk0 = f_fvg_idx(fz_his, fz_los, math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2), math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2))
                if uk0 >= 0
                    f_fvg_drop(fz_his, fz_los, fz_x, fz_xb, fz_p, uk0)
            else if not na(retest_lvl)
                array.push(d_used, retest_lvl)
                if array.size(d_used) > 300
                    array.shift(d_used)
            if (retest_src == "post_breakout_fvg" or retest_src == "inside_fvg") and array.size(fz_his) > 0
                float uh = math.max(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
                float ul = math.min(retest_lvl, retest_lvl2)
                int uk = array.size(fz_his) - 1
                while uk >= 0
                    float UH = array.get(fz_his, uk)
                    float UL = array.get(fz_los, uk)
                    if (fz_bull ? UL > uh : UH < ul) and f_bt_seen(fz_bull ? UH : UL)
                        f_fvg_drop(fz_his, fz_los, fz_x, fz_xb, fz_p, uk)
                    uk -= 1
            retest_on  := false
            retest_src := na
            retest_lvl := na
            retest_lvl2 := na
            anchor_lvl := na

    // ── H4 Continuation block ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    if h4_bo_fired
        // Out of line: an H4 break AGAINST the daily bias — a close below the
        // latest H4 V-shape in a buy, above the latest H4 A-shape in a sell
        // (same test as a confirmation, no tolerance). Every H4 OC is dropped.
        // H4 comes back in line only through a fresh daily reaction followed by
        // an H4 break in the daily direction (H4 CONFIRMED block above).
        if h4_aligned
            bool against = (bo_dir == "bullish" and not na(h4_v_lvl) and not new_v and close < h4_v_lvl) or (bo_dir == "bearish" and not na(h4_a_lvl) and not new_a and close > h4_a_lvl)
            if against
                h4_aligned    := false
                array.clear(h4_ocs)
                array.clear(h4_ocb)

        // A new H4 breakout in the daily direction while in line (a close beyond
        // the latest H4 A for buys / V for sells, not the level already broken):
        // it alerts, its level becomes the H4 Breaker (replacing the older one)
        // and only the OCs of its leg (from its swing low/high) and after it count.
        if h4_aligned and not confirmed_this_bar
            bool  ilb     = bo_dir == "bullish"
            float brk_lvl = ilb ? h4_a_lvl : h4_v_lvl
            bool  brk     = not na(brk_lvl) and (ilb ? (not new_a and close > brk_lvl) : (not new_v and close < brk_lvl)) and (na(h4_brk_lvl) or brk_lvl != h4_brk_lvl)
            if brk
                h4_brk_lvl            := brk_lvl
                h4_breaker_lvl        := brk_lvl
                bk_origin             := bar_index
                h4_invalid_lvl        := ilb ? h4_v_lvl : h4_a_lvl
                h4_breaker_orig_fired := false
                f_h4_leg_prune(h4_ocs, h4_ocb, ilb ? h4a_origin : h4v_origin, ilb)
                f_rt_arm(ilb, ilb ? h4a_origin : h4v_origin, brk_lvl)
                confirmed_this_bar    := true
                f_btlbl(ilb, 2, "", brk_lvl, bo_level, "")
                if barstate.isrealtime
                    alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                          + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"inline_break"'
                          + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                          + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(brk_lvl) + '}',
                          alert.freq_once_per_bar)

        if confirmed_this_bar
            h4f_bar  := bar_index
            h4f_bull := bo_dir == "bullish"
            h4f_ref  := h4f_bull ? high[1] : low[1]

        if h4_aligned and not confirmed_this_bar
            if not na(h4_breaker_lvl)
                // Re-arm when a NEW breaker level is established
                if na(bk_armed_lvl) or bk_armed_lvl != h4_breaker_lvl
                    bk_armed     := true
                    bk_armed_lvl := h4_breaker_lvl
                bool bk_touched = low <= h4_breaker_lvl and high >= h4_breaker_lvl
                // Only the first touch of an H4 Breaker counts: it alerts if it is a
                // rejection, and either way the Breaker is used (no later retests)
                // A rejection comes INTO the level from the bias side: for a buy the
                // candle opens at/above it, dips in and closes above (mirror for sells).
                // A candle climbing up through it from below is not a rejection.
                bool bk_react = bk_armed and bk_touched and ((bo_dir == "bullish" and open >= h4_breaker_lvl and close > h4_breaker_lvl) or (bo_dir == "bearish" and open <= h4_breaker_lvl and close < h4_breaker_lvl))
                if bk_touched
                    bk_armed := false
                if bk_react
                    string bk_type = h4_breaker_orig_fired ? "breaker_cont" : "breaker_origin"
                    if not h4_breaker_orig_fired
                        h4_breaker_orig_fired := true
                    bk_armed := false
                    bk_sent  := true
                    f_btlbl(bo_dir == "bullish", bk_type == "breaker_origin" ? 3 : 4, "", h4_breaker_lvl, bo_level, "")
                    if barstate.isrealtime
                        alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                              + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"' + bk_type + '"'
                              + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                              + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(h4_breaker_lvl) + '}',
                              alert.freq_once_per_bar)

    // ── Retest that held (for "H4 OC only after a retest that held") ──────
    // An H4 candle after the breakout touches the Breaker or one of the leg's
    // V-shapes (A-shapes for sells) and closes back beyond it.
    if h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned and not confirmed_this_bar and not array.get(rt_held, 0) and array.size(rt_lvls) > 0
        for rl in rt_lvls
            if bo_dir == "bullish" ? (low <= rl and close > rl) : (high >= rl and close < rl)
                array.set(rt_held, 0, true)
                break
    bool oc_rt = array.get(rt_held, 0)

    // ── H4 OCs (trend continuation) ───────────────────────────────────────
    bool ocb = bo_dir == "bullish"
    // a) New in-line H4 breakouts prune the list in the continuation block above.
    // b) Rejections, checked against the OCs that existed BEFORE this candle:
    //    opens on the bias side, wick touches the exact level, closes beyond it.
    //    One alert naming the furthest OC reached; every OC it rejected is used
    //    and removed. An OC closed through the wrong way is removed too.
    float oc_hit = na
    int   k = array.size(h4_ocs) - 1
    while k >= 0
        float L = array.get(h4_ocs, k)
        if array.get(h4_ocb, k) < bar_index
            bool react = low <= L and high >= L and (ocb ? (open >= L and close > L) : (open <= L and close < L))
            bool dead  = ocb ? close < L : close > L
            if react and h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned and not confirmed_this_bar
                oc_hit := na(oc_hit) ? L : ocb ? math.min(oc_hit, L) : math.max(oc_hit, L)
                array.remove(h4_ocs, k)
                array.remove(h4_ocb, k)
            else if dead or (low <= L and high >= L)   // touched without a rejection: used
                array.remove(h4_ocs, k)
                array.remove(h4_ocb, k)
        k -= 1
    if not na(oc_hit) and (oc_rt or not bt_oc_rt)
        f_btlbl(ocb, 5, "", oc_hit, bo_level, oc_rt ? "After a retest that held" : "")
    if not na(oc_hit) and barstate.isrealtime
        alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
              + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"oc_cont","after_retest":' + (oc_rt ? "true" : "false")
              + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
              + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(oc_hit) + '}',
              alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    // d) Engulfing in the Daily direction (after the Origin, while in line): the
    //    candle covers the previous opposite candle's BODY (buy: previous
    //    bearish; this one opens at/below its close and closes above its open).
    //    eng_wick = it also closes beyond that candle's wick (buy: above its HIGH).
    //    Each subscriber picks wick / body-only / both on the server.
    //    One alert per candle: not when another continuation fired on it.
    if h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned and not confirmed_this_bar and not bk_sent and na(oc_hit)
        bool eng = ocb ? (close[1] < open[1] and close > open and open <= close[1] and close > open[1])
                       : (close[1] > open[1] and close < open and open >= close[1] and close < open[1])
        bool eng_wick = ocb ? close > high[1] : close < low[1]
        if eng and (bt_eng_mode != "Wick" or eng_wick)
            bool  hwb    = f_eng_wickbox(bt_eng_mode, eng_wick)
            float hb_top = hwb or not ocb ? high[1] : math.max(open[1], close[1])   // the covered H4 candle
            float hb_bot = hwb or ocb ? low[1] : math.min(open[1], close[1])
            string htip = (ocb ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " · H4 engulfing\n" + (eng_wick ? "Covers the previous candle's wick" : "Covers the previous candle's body only")
            if f_btlbl(ocb, 6, "", eng_wick ? (ocb ? high[1] : low[1]) : open[1], bo_level, eng_wick ? "Covers the previous candle's wick" : "Covers the previous candle's body only")
                f_eng_draw(false, time[1], time, hb_top, hb_bot, htip)
            // The same test as the chart label, without the label code: this boxed
            // engulfing is what the charts below 4H draw
            if bt_show and bt_engulf and time >= bt_from and (e4_cls == "" or (e4_cls == "external" ? bt_ext : bt_int))
                e4_n   += 1
                e4_t1  := time[1]
                e4_top := hb_top
                e4_bot := hb_bot
                e4_tip := htip
        if eng and barstate.isrealtime
            alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                  + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"engulfing","eng_wick":' + (eng_wick ? "true" : "false")
                  + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                  + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(eng_wick ? (ocb ? high[1] : low[1]) : open[1]) + '}',
                  alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    // c) Record a new OC: two H4 candles in a row in the daily direction; the
    //    level is where the first one closed.
    if ocb ? (h4_bull1 and h4_bull0) : (h4_bear1 and h4_bear0)
        array.push(h4_ocs, close[1])
        array.push(h4_ocb, bar_index)
        if array.size(h4_ocs) > 40
            array.shift(h4_ocs)
            array.shift(h4_ocb)
        // OC formed notification (no buy / sell): after the Origin, while in line
        if h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned
            if bt_hocf and time >= bt_from and (oc_rt or not bt_oc_rt)
                label.delete(ocf_h)
                ocf_h := label.new(bar_index, ocb ? low : high, "✕", yloc=ocb ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
                     style=label.style_none, textcolor=bt_ocf_col, size=size.small,
                     tooltip=syminfo.ticker + "\nH4 OC has formed\nOC level " + str.tostring(close[1], format.mintick))
            if barstate.isrealtime
                alert(f_hdrw("H4_CONTINUATION")
                      + '","direction":"' + bo_dir + '","cont_type":"h4_oc_formed","after_retest":' + (oc_rt ? "true" : "false")
                      + ',"level_type":"' + bo_layer + '","breakout_level":' + str.tostring(bo_level)
                      + ',"h4_level":' + str.tostring(close[1]) + '}',
                      alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── H4 engulfing boxes below the 4H chart: the same ones as on the 4H chart ──
// The H4 steps run on 4H candles here too; [1] + lookahead_on = state after the
// last COMPLETED H4 candle (no repaint). A new count = a new boxed H4 engulfing.
[r4_n, r4_t1, r4_top, r4_bot, r4_tip] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "240",
     [e4_n[1], e4_t1[1], e4_top[1], e4_bot[1], e4_tip[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
if timeframe.in_seconds() < 14400 and not na(r4_n) and r4_n > nz(r4_n[1]) and not na(r4_t1)
    f_eng_draw(false, r4_t1, time[1], r4_top, r4_bot, r4_tip)

// Newest watched H4 OC, for the label, line and dashboard snapshot
float h4c_oc_lvl = array.size(h4_ocs) > 0 ? array.get(h4_ocs, array.size(h4_ocs) - 1) : na
h4c_origin := array.size(h4_ocb) > 0 ? array.get(h4_ocb, array.size(h4_ocb) - 1) : na

// ── Visual overlays ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── Right-edge level labels ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var label _a_lbl   = na
var label _wbk_lbl = na
var label _wav_lbl = na
var label _woc_lbl = na
var label _v_lbl   = na
var label _h4a_lbl = na
var label _h4v_lbl = na
var label _poc_lbl = na
var label _bk_lbl  = na
var label _h4c_lbl = na

var line _a_line   = na
var line _v_line   = na
var line _h4a_line = na
var line _h4v_line = na
var line _poc_line = na
var line _bk_line  = na
var line _h4c_line = na

label.delete(_a_lbl)
label.delete(_v_lbl)
label.delete(_h4a_lbl)
label.delete(_h4v_lbl)
label.delete(_poc_lbl)
label.delete(_bk_lbl)
label.delete(_h4c_lbl)

line.delete(_a_line)
line.delete(_v_line)
line.delete(_h4a_line)
line.delete(_h4v_line)
line.delete(_poc_line)
line.delete(_bk_line)
line.delete(_h4c_line)

label.delete(_wbk_lbl)
label.delete(_wav_lbl)
label.delete(_woc_lbl)
if barstate.islast
    int lbl_x = bar_index + 20
    if bt_weekly and show_wk_lbls and show_wk_on_tf and not na(wk_dir)
        color wtxt = color.new(color.black, 0)
        _wbk_lbl := label.new(lbl_x + 14, wk_level, "W.BK  " + str.tostring(wk_level, "#.#####") + (wk_react ? "  (reacting)" : ""), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(wk_col, 30), textcolor=wtxt, size=size.small)
        float wav = wk_dir == "bullish" ? w_dv : w_da
        if not na(wav)
            _wav_lbl := label.new(lbl_x + 14, wav, (wk_dir == "bullish" ? "W.V  " : "W.A  ") + str.tostring(wav, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(wk_col, 50), textcolor=wtxt, size=size.small)
        if not na(wpb_oc_lvl)
            _woc_lbl := label.new(lbl_x + 14, wpb_oc_lvl, "W.OC  " + str.tostring(wpb_oc_lvl, "#.#####") + (array.size(w_pbocs) > 1 ? "  (" + str.tostring(array.size(w_pbocs)) + " watched)" : ""), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(wk_col, 50), textcolor=wtxt, size=size.small)
    if show_daily_lbls and show_daily_on_tf
        if not na(a_lvl)
            _a_lbl   := label.new(lbl_x, a_lvl,     "D.A  " + str.tostring(a_lvl,     "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=da_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        if not na(v_lvl)
            _v_lbl   := label.new(lbl_x, v_lvl,     "D.V  " + str.tostring(v_lvl,     "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=dv_lbl_col, textcolor=color.black, size=size.small)
        if not na(pb_oc_lvl)
            _poc_lbl := label.new(lbl_x, pb_oc_lvl, "D.OC " + str.tostring(pb_oc_lvl, "#.#####") + (array.size(pb_ocs) > 1 ? "  (" + str.tostring(array.size(pb_ocs)) + " watched)" : ""), style=label.style_label_left, color=doc_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    if show_h4_lbls and show_h4_on_tf
        if not na(h4_a_lvl)
            _h4a_lbl := label.new(lbl_x, h4_a_lvl,       "H4.A  " + str.tostring(h4_a_lvl,       "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=h4a_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        if not na(h4_v_lvl)
            _h4v_lbl := label.new(lbl_x, h4_v_lvl,       "H4.V  " + str.tostring(h4_v_lvl,       "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=h4v_lbl_col, textcolor=color.black, size=size.small)
        if not na(h4_breaker_lvl)
            _bk_lbl  := label.new(lbl_x, h4_breaker_lvl, "H4.BK " + str.tostring(h4_breaker_lvl, "#.#####"), style=label.style_label_left, color=h4bk_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        if not na(h4c_oc_lvl)
            _h4c_lbl := label.new(lbl_x, h4c_oc_lvl,     "H4.OC " + str.tostring(h4c_oc_lvl,     "#.#####") + (array.size(h4_ocs) > 1 ? "  (" + str.tostring(array.size(h4_ocs)) + " watched)" : ""), style=label.style_label_left, color=h4oc_lbl_col, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    // Second point one step right of the first: a line whose level formed on the
    // current candle would otherwise have no direction and extend straight down.
    if show_lvl_lines
        if show_daily_on_tf and not na(a_lvl)          and not na(s_da_t)
            _a_line   := line.new(s_da_t,     a_lvl,          s_da_t + timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000, a_lvl,          xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right, color=daily_line_col, width=1)
        if show_daily_on_tf and not na(v_lvl)          and not na(s_dv_t)
            _v_line   := line.new(s_dv_t,     v_lvl,          s_dv_t + timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000, v_lvl,          xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right, color=daily_line_col, width=1)
        if show_daily_on_tf and not na(pb_oc_lvl)      and not na(poc_origin)
            _poc_line := line.new(poc_origin, pb_oc_lvl,      poc_origin + 1, pb_oc_lvl,      extend=extend.right, color=daily_line_col, width=1)
        if show_h4_on_tf and not na(h4_a_lvl)       and not na(h4a_origin)
            _h4a_line := line.new(h4a_origin, h4_a_lvl,       h4a_origin + 1, h4_a_lvl,       extend=extend.right, color=h4_line_col,    width=1)
        if show_h4_on_tf and not na(h4_v_lvl)       and not na(h4v_origin)
            _h4v_line := line.new(h4v_origin, h4_v_lvl,       h4v_origin + 1, h4_v_lvl,       extend=extend.right, color=h4_line_col,    width=1)
        if show_h4_on_tf and not na(h4_breaker_lvl) and not na(bk_origin)
            _bk_line  := line.new(bk_origin,  h4_breaker_lvl, bk_origin + 1, h4_breaker_lvl, extend=extend.right, color=h4_line_col,    width=1)
        if show_h4_on_tf and not na(h4c_oc_lvl)     and not na(h4c_origin)
            _h4c_line := line.new(h4c_origin, h4c_oc_lvl,     h4c_origin + 1, h4c_oc_lvl,     extend=extend.right, color=h4_line_col,    width=1)

// ── Daily structure levels on the chart ──────────────────────────────────────
var array<line>  _st_lines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label> _st_labels = array.new<label>()

f_draw_lvl(bool show, int t1, float y, string txt, color c, string st, int w) =>
    if show and not na(y) and not na(t1)
        int t2 = time + 5 * timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000
        array.push(_st_lines, line.new(t1, y, t2, y, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c, style = f_style(st), width = w))
        array.push(_st_labels, label.new(bar_index + 6, y, txt + "  " + str.tostring(y, format.mintick),
          style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = bt_ext_txt, size = size.small))

f_dirw(string d) =>
    d == "bull" ? "Bullish " : "Bearish "

if barstate.islast
    for ln in _st_lines
        line.delete(ln)
    for lb in _st_labels
        label.delete(lb)
    array.clear(_st_lines)
    array.clear(_st_labels)
    if show_daily_on_tf and not na(s_cdir) and s_cdir != "none"
        string forming = " (still forming)"
        f_draw_lvl(show_ext, s_chit, s_chi, f_dirw(s_cdir) + "External high" + (s_cdir == "bull" and not s_chif ? forming : ""), c_eh, s_eh, w_ext)
        f_draw_lvl(show_ext, s_clot, s_clo, f_dirw(s_cdir) + "External low" + (s_cdir == "bear" and not s_clof ? forming : ""), c_el, s_el, w_ext)
    if bt_weekly and show_wk_ext and show_wk_on_tf and not na(w_cdir) and w_cdir != "none"
        string wforming = " (still forming)"
        f_draw_lvl(true, w_chit, w_chi, f_dirw(w_cdir) + "Weekly External high" + (w_cdir == "bull" and not w_chif ? wforming : ""), wk_col, wk_style, wk_width)
        f_draw_lvl(true, w_clot, w_clo, f_dirw(w_cdir) + "Weekly External low" + (w_cdir == "bear" and not w_clof ? wforming : ""), wk_col, wk_style, wk_width)

// ── State label — shows script's current understanding at the latest bar ──────
f_src_name(string src, string kind) =>
    src == "daily_breaker" ? "Daily Breaker" : src == "post_breakout_oc" ? "post-breakout Daily OC" : src == "post_breakout_fvg" ? "Daily FVG after the breakout" : src == "inside_fvg" ? "Daily FVG inside the range" : kind == "oc" ? "Daily OC" : kind == "a_shape" ? "Daily A-shape" : "Daily V-shape"

string _state_txt = "IDLE - no breakout detected"
if not na(bo_dir) and not h4_bo_fired and retest_on
    _state_txt := (bo_dir == "bullish" ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " Retest | " + retest_src
else if not na(bo_dir) and not h4_bo_fired
    _state_txt := "BREAKOUT | " + bo_dir + " (" + f_layer_name(bo_layer) + ") | awaiting retest" + ((bo_dir == "bullish" ? est_above : est_below) ? "" : " · price hasn't moved away from the breakout yet")
else if h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned
    _state_txt := "CONFIRMED | " + bo_dir + " | H4 aligned" + (retest_on ? "\nDaily reaction at " + f_bt_src(retest_src) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(retest_lvl) + " · waiting for H4 External breakout " + (bo_dir == "bullish" ? "above " + str.tostring(bt_ext_a, format.mintick) : "below " + str.tostring(bt_ext_v, format.mintick)) : "")
else if h4_bo_fired
    _state_txt := retest_on
         ? "OUT OF LINE | daily " + bo_dir + " | reacting at " + f_src_name(retest_src, retest_kind) + " @ " + f_bt_lvtxt(retest_lvl) + " · waiting for H4 External breakout " + (bo_dir == "bullish" ? "above " + str.tostring(bt_ext_a, format.mintick) : "below " + str.tostring(bt_ext_v, format.mintick))
         : "OUT OF LINE | daily " + bo_dir + " | H4 broke " + (bo_dir == "bullish" ? "bearish" : "bullish") + " · waiting for a daily reaction, then an H4 " + bo_dir + " break" + ((bo_dir == "bullish" ? est_above : est_below) ? "" : " (price hasn't moved away from the breakout yet)")
// Off the 4H chart, show only what the DAILY candles decided (direction and the
// broken level) — the H4 steps would run on the wrong candles there.
string _wk_txt = not bt_weekly or na(wk_dir) ? "" : "\nWEEKLY " + wk_dir + (wk_react ? " · reacting at " + f_wsrc_name(wk_src, wk_kind) + " @ " + str.tostring(wk_src_lvl, "#.#####") : "")
     + (bo_wk_rel == "confirmed" ? " · Daily " + bo_wk_cls + " breakout Weekly-confirmed" : bo_wk_rel == "against" ? " · Daily is AGAINST the Weekly" : "")
bool _is_4h = timeframe.period == "240"
if not _is_4h
    _state_txt := na(bo_dir) ? "DAILY | no breakout" : "DAILY | BREAKOUT | " + bo_dir + " (" + f_layer_name(bo_layer) + ") @ " + str.tostring(bo_level, "#.#####") + " | check 4H"

// ── Price feed + chart snapshot — fires at every realtime H4 close ───────────
// Powers dashboard price-level alerts and the server's copy of this chart's
// state and levels (so the dashboard matches the chart even for setups that
// formed before the script was pasted).
string _stage = na(bo_dir) ? "idle" : retest_on ? "retest" : not h4_bo_fired ? "breakout" : h4_aligned ? "confirmed_aligned" : "confirmed_realigning"
if barstate.isconfirmed and barstate.isrealtime
    alert(f_hdr("PRICE_UPDATE")
          + '","price":' + str.tostring(close)
          + ',"snapshot":{"stage":"' + _stage + '"'
          + ',"bias":' + (na(bo_dir) ? "null" : '"' + bo_dir + '"')
          + ',"retest_source":' + (na(retest_src) ? "null" : '"' + retest_src + '"')
          + ',"breakout_level":' + f_num(bo_level)
          + ',"level_type":' + (na(bo_layer) ? "null" : '"' + bo_layer + '"')
          + ',"ext_hi":' + f_num(s_chi) + ',"ext_lo":' + f_num(s_clo)
          + ',"d_a":' + f_num(a_lvl) + ',"d_v":' + f_num(v_lvl)
          + ',"d_oc":' + f_num(pb_oc_lvl) + ',"d_oc_count":' + str.tostring(array.size(pb_ocs))
          + ',"h4_a":' + f_num(h4_a_lvl) + ',"h4_v":' + f_num(h4_v_lvl)
          + ',"h4_bk":' + f_num(h4_breaker_lvl) + ',"h4_oc":' + f_num(h4c_oc_lvl)
          + ',"wk_dir":' + (na(wk_dir) ? "null" : '"' + wk_dir + '"')
          + ',"wk_react":' + (wk_react ? "true" : "false")
          + ',"wk_src":' + (wk_react ? '"' + f_wsrc_name(wk_src, wk_kind) + '"' : "null")
          + ',"wk_src_lvl":' + f_num(wk_react ? wk_src_lvl : na)
          + ',"wk_rel":"' + bo_wk_rel + '"'
          + ',"wk_cls":' + (bo_wk_rel == "confirmed" ? '"' + bo_wk_cls + '"' : "null")
          + ',"w_hi":' + f_num(w_chi) + ',"w_lo":' + f_num(w_clo)
          + ',"w_bk":' + f_num(wk_level)
          + ',"w_av":' + f_num(na(wk_dir) ? na : wk_dir == "bullish" ? w_dv : w_da)
          + ',"w_oc":' + f_num(wpb_oc_lvl) + '}'
          + ',"bar":' + f_bar(time, open, high, low, close)
          + ',"dbar":' + f_bar(dr_t, dr_o, dr_h, dr_l, dr_c) + '}',
          alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── Candle history for the server's chart pictures ───────────────────────────
// Once per alert: the first realtime H4 close sends the last Daily candles, the
// second the last H4 candles. From then on every PRICE_UPDATE carries the
// candle that just closed and the last completed Daily candle.
var int hist_step = 0
if barstate.isconfirmed and barstate.isrealtime and hist_step < 2
    string js = ""
    if hist_step == 0
        int nd = array.size(dh_t)
        if nd > 0
            for i = 0 to nd - 1
                js := js + (i > 0 ? "," : "") + f_bar(array.get(dh_t, i), array.get(dh_o, i), array.get(dh_h, i), array.get(dh_l, i), array.get(dh_c, i))
            alert(f_hdr("HISTORY") + '","tf":"D","bars":[' + js + ']}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    else
        int nh = math.min(HIST_N, bar_index)
        for i = nh - 1 to 0
            js := js + (i < nh - 1 ? "," : "") + f_bar(time[i], open[i], high[i], low[i], close[i])
        alert(f_hdr("HISTORY") + '","tf":"' + timeframe.period + '","bars":[' + js + ']}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    hist_step += 1


color _lbl_col = idle_lbl_col
if retest_on
    _lbl_col := retest_lbl_col
else if h4_bo_fired and h4_aligned
    _lbl_col := conf_lbl_col
else if h4_bo_fired
    _lbl_col := realign_lbl_col
else if bo_dir == "bullish"
    _lbl_col := bull_lbl_col
else if bo_dir == "bearish"
    _lbl_col := bear_lbl_col
if not _is_4h
    _lbl_col := na(bo_dir) ? idle_lbl_col : bo_dir == "bullish" ? bull_lbl_col : bear_lbl_col

var label _state_lbl = na
label.delete(_state_lbl)
string _tip = "bo=" + str.tostring(bo_level, "#.#####") + " (" + f_layer_name(bo_layer) + ") range=" + str.tostring(bo_opp, "#.#####") + " D.A=" + str.tostring(a_lvl, "#.#####") + " D.V=" + str.tostring(v_lvl, "#.#####") + " D.OC=" + str.tostring(pb_oc_lvl, "#.#####") + " H4.A=" + str.tostring(h4_a_lvl, "#.#####") + " H4.V=" + str.tostring(h4_v_lvl, "#.#####") + " H4.BK=" + str.tostring(h4_breaker_lvl, "#.#####") + " H4.OC=" + str.tostring(h4c_oc_lvl, "#.#####")
if bt_marks == "Full labels"
    _state_lbl := label.new(bar_index, high, _state_txt + _wk_txt, style=label.style_label_down, color=_lbl_col, textcolor=bt_state_txt, size=size.small, tooltip=_tip)

// ── Info table: status + the latest alert, at the side so the candles stay clear ─
f_info_pos(string p) =>
    switch p
        "Top right"    => position.top_right
        "Bottom right" => position.bottom_right
        "Top left"     => position.top_left
        "Middle left"  => position.middle_left
        "Bottom left"  => position.bottom_left
        => position.middle_right
var table bt_info_tbl = table.new(f_info_pos(bt_info_pos), 1, 4, bgcolor=bt_tbl_bg, border_width=1, border_color=color.new(color.gray, 70))
if barstate.islast and bt_marks == "Circle + info table" and bt_info_on
    table.cell(bt_info_tbl, 0, 0, "Status", text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(bt_info_tbl, 0, 1, str.replace_all(str.replace_all(_state_txt + _wk_txt, " · ", "\n"), " | ", "\n"),
         text_color=bt_tbl_txt, bgcolor=color.new(_lbl_col, 65), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    if _is_4h and array.get(bt_info, 0) != ""
        table.cell(bt_info_tbl, 0, 2, "Latest confirmation alert · " + array.get(bt_info, 1), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(bt_info_tbl, 0, 3, array.get(bt_info, 0), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)

// ── Backtest count ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The count table sits top right, or bottom right when the info table is there
var table bt_tbl = bt_table ? table.new(bt_marks == "Circle + info table" and bt_info_pos == "Top right" ? position.bottom_right : position.top_right, 2, 14,
     bgcolor=bt_tbl_bg, border_width=1, border_color=color.new(color.gray, 70)) : na
if bt_table and barstate.islast and timeframe.period != "240"
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 0, "Backtest labels show on the 4H chart only", text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small)
if bt_table and barstate.islast and timeframe.period == "240"
    int bt_total = array.get(bt_cnt, 8) + array.get(bt_cnt, 9)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 0, "H4 aligned alerts", text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 0, str.tostring(bt_total), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.small)
    for i = 0 to 7
        table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, i + 1, array.get(BT_NAMES, i), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
        table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, i + 1, str.tostring(array.get(bt_cnt, i)), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 12, array.get(BT_NAMES, 10), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 12, str.tostring(array.get(bt_cnt, 10)), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 13, array.get(BT_NAMES, 11), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 13, str.tostring(array.get(bt_cnt, 11)), text_color=bt_tbl_txt, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 9, "Buys", text_color=bt_buy_col, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 9, str.tostring(array.get(bt_cnt, 8)), text_color=bt_buy_col, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 10, "Sells", text_color=bt_sell_col, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 10, str.tostring(array.get(bt_cnt, 9)), text_color=bt_sell_col, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 0, 11, "Since", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(bt_tbl, 1, 11, str.format_time(math.max(bt_from, bt_t0), "dd MMM yyyy"), text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny)

// ── Backtest: the Daily reaction levels being watched right now ──────────────
var array<line>  bt_lv_lines = array.new<line>()
var array<label> bt_lv_lbls  = array.new<label>()
var array<box>   bt_fvg_bxs  = array.new<box>()
f_bt_fvg(float H, float L, string txt) =>
    if array.size(bt_fvg_bxs) < 20
        array.push(bt_fvg_bxs, box.new(bar_index - 40, H, bar_index + 3, L, border_color=bt_fvg_col, bgcolor=bt_fvg_col,
             text=txt + "  " + str.tostring(L, format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(H, format.mintick),
             text_color=bt_lv_col, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right))
f_bt_lv(float y, string txt) =>
    if not na(y) and array.size(bt_lv_lines) < 30
        array.push(bt_lv_lines, line.new(bar_index - 40, y, bar_index + 3, y, color=bt_lv_col, style=line.style_dotted))
        array.push(bt_lv_lbls, label.new(bar_index + 3, y, txt + "  " + str.tostring(y, format.mintick),
             style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor=bt_lv_col, size=size.small))
if barstate.islast
    for ln in bt_lv_lines
        line.delete(ln)
    for lb in bt_lv_lbls
        label.delete(lb)
    array.clear(bt_lv_lines)
    array.clear(bt_lv_lbls)
    for bx in bt_fvg_bxs
        box.delete(bx)
    array.clear(bt_fvg_bxs)
    if bt_lvls and timeframe.period == "240" and not na(bo_dir) and not na(bo_level)
        bool bb = bo_dir == "bullish"
        f_bt_lv(bo_level, "Daily Breaker")
        for L in pb_ocs
            f_bt_lv(L, "Daily OC after the breakout")
        array<float> shp = bb ? d_vs : d_as
        for L in shp
            if bb ? L > bo_level + tol : L < bo_level - tol
                f_bt_lv(L, bb ? "Daily V-shape after the breakout" : "Daily A-shape after the breakout")
            else if not na(bo_opp) and (bb ? (L > bo_opp and L < bo_level - tol) : (L < bo_opp and L > bo_level + tol))
                f_bt_lv(L, bb ? "Daily V-shape inside the range" : "Daily A-shape inside the range")
        array<float> ocs = bb ? d_boc : d_soc
        for L in ocs
            if not na(bo_opp) and (bb ? (L > bo_opp and L < bo_level - tol) : (L < bo_opp and L > bo_level + tol))
                f_bt_lv(L, "Daily OC inside the range")
        if bt_dfvg
            array<float> fhs = bb ? d_bf_hi : d_sf_hi
            array<float> fls = bb ? d_bf_lo : d_sf_lo
            if array.size(fhs) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(fhs) - 1
                    float H = array.get(fhs, i)
                    float L = array.get(fls, i)
                    if array.get(bb ? d_bf_p : d_sf_p, i)
                        continue
                    if bb ? H > bo_level + tol : L < bo_level - tol
                        f_bt_fvg(H, L, "Daily FVG after the breakout")
                    else if not na(bo_opp) and (bb ? (L > bo_opp and H < bo_level - tol) : (H < bo_opp and L > bo_level + tol))
                        f_bt_fvg(H, L, "Daily FVG inside the range")
